window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/courses/b012-8792adfa4865abcb.json"]={sha256:"8792adfa4865abcbc74a0425455abc7bfa88aaf3144378ed1c70746cef7fb338",value:{"id":"b012","title":"里翁—安提里翁大橋","titleEn":"Rion–Antirion Bridge","category":"structures","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"里翁—安提里翁大橋以 286+3×560+286 m 共 2,252 m 的連續全懸吊橋面跨越希臘科林斯灣口，四座塔立在直徑 90 m、坐於 3 m 礫石層上的基礎，下方以 2 m 鋼管插入物加勁軟弱海床。本課從 0.48 g 地震與 2 m 斷層位移、熔斷限制器與黏滯阻尼器、加勁土壤與沉箱浮運，到張力腿駁船的海床整備、平衡懸臂架設、WEASHM 監測、雷擊斷索與混凝土耐久。","summaryEn":"The Rion–Antirion Bridge crosses the mouth of the Gulf of Corinth with a 2,252 m continuous fully suspended deck of 286+3×560+286 m; its four pylons stand on 90 m diameter footings resting on a 3 m gravel layer above soft seabed reinforced with 2 m steel-pipe inclusions. The course runs from 0.48 g shaking and 2 m fault movement, fuse restrainers and viscous dampers, reinforced soil and floating caissons, to seabed preparation from a tension-leg barge, balanced-cantilever erection, the WEASHM monitoring system, the lightning-caused stay failure and concrete durability.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、吊裝或張拉作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, lifting or stressing permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"st-cable-stayed","subcategoryTitle":"斜張橋與斜索系統","subcategoryTitleEn":"Cable-stayed bridges and stay systems","learningTrack":"structures","learningSubdiscipline":"st-cable-stayed","learningTags":["structures","st-cable-stayed","cablestayed"],"architectureFamily":"cablestayed","architectureNodes":[["加勁土壤與礫石層","Reinforced soil and gravel bed"],["90 m 基礎與四腿塔","90 m footings and four-legged pylons"],["鋼絞線斜索","Strand stay cables"],["連續全懸吊組合橋面","Continuous suspended composite deck"],["熔斷限制器與阻尼器","Fuse restrainers and dampers"],["WEASHM 監測與測地","WEASHM monitoring and geodesy"]],"architectureEdges":[[1,0],[2,1],[3,2],[3,4],[4,1],[4,5],[1,5]],"diagram":{"type":"cablestayed","labels":["加勁土壤與礫石層","90 m 基礎與四腿塔","鋼絞線斜索","連續全懸吊組合橋面","熔斷限制器與阻尼器"],"labelsEn":["Reinforced soil and gravel bed","90 m footings and four-legged pylons","Strand stay cables","Continuous suspended composite deck","Fuse restrainers and dampers"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"設計練習：比較一座 90 m 基礎在地震中「不滑移」與「可滑移」時傳到上部結構的水平力。設基礎與塔座、墩身的有效質量 M = 80,000 t，若完全固定，以譜加速度 1.2 g 估算慣性力 F = M·S_a = 80,000×1.2×9.81 ≈ 941,800 kN。若基礎坐在礫石層上、摩擦係數 μ = tan35° ≈ 0.70、有效垂直力 N = 600,000 kN（扣除浮力），滑移前最大水平力 H = μ·N ≈ 420,000 kN，只有固定時的 420,000/941,800 ≈ 45%。代價是滑移位移：若地震造成 0.5 m 永久滑移，需確認伸縮縫與阻尼器的位移預算仍足夠（主墩阻尼器行程 −1,650 至 +1,850 mm）。若礫石摩擦角改為 30°（tan30° ≈ 0.577），H ≈ 346,400 kN，力量更低但滑移量會增加。質量、垂直力與摩擦角為教學假設，非本橋設計值。","textEn":"Design exercise: compare the horizontal force passed to the superstructure by a 90 m footing that cannot slide with one that can. Take an effective mass of footing, base and shaft M = 80,000 t; if fully fixed, a spectral acceleration of 1.2 g gives an inertia force F = M·S_a = 80,000×1.2×9.81 ≈ 941,800 kN. If the footing rests on gravel with friction coefficient μ = tan35° ≈ 0.70 and effective vertical force N = 600,000 kN after buoyancy, the largest horizontal force before sliding is H = μ·N ≈ 420,000 kN, only 420,000/941,800 ≈ 45% of the fixed case. The price is sliding displacement: if the earthquake leaves 0.5 m of permanent slip, the displacement budget of joints and dampers must still suffice (main-pier damper stroke −1,650 to +1,850 mm). With a 30° gravel friction angle (tan30° ≈ 0.577), H ≈ 346,400 kN, a lower force but more sliding. Mass, vertical force and friction angle are teaching assumptions, not design values for this bridge.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":13,"enrichmentVersion":13,"stages":[{"id":"b012-v13-s1","title":"工程背景、荷載與結構系統","titleEn":"Context, loads and structural system","description":"本階段聚焦「地震、斷層與海峽擴張的設計需求」與「連續全懸吊橋面：熔斷限制器與黏滯阻尼器」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Design demands from earthquakes, faults and a widening strait\" and \"Continuous suspended deck: fuse restrainers and viscous dampers\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b012-v13-01","title":"地震、斷層與海峽擴張的設計需求：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Design demands from earthquakes, faults and a widening strait: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「墩間相對位移」如何影響里翁—安提里翁大橋的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Relative pier movement” governs force, deformation or durability in “Rion–Antirion Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"橋址位於構造活躍的科林斯灣，營運單位公開的設計條件包括：地表尖峰加速度 0.48 g、0.2 至 1.0 s 週期的最大譜加速度 1.2 g、回歸期 2,000 年（120 年設計年限內 5% 超越機率），且相鄰橋墩之間須容許任何方向達 2 m 的斷層相對位移，塔的傾斜容許 1/500。這些需求使傳統「把結構牢牢固定」的做法行不通：基礎必須能在海床上滑移，橋面必須與塔分離懸吊，讓地震與構造位移由可控制的滑動、擺動與阻尼吸收，而不是由構件強度硬抗。最不利的設計組合是設計地震加上 50% 的構造位移。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「墩間相對位移」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The site lies in the tectonically active Gulf of Corinth. The operator’s published design criteria include a peak ground acceleration of 0.48 g, maximum spectral acceleration of 1.2 g for periods of 0.2 to 1.0 s, a 2,000-year return period (5% exceedance in the 120-year design life), up to 2 m of fault movement in any direction between adjacent piers and a pylon tilt allowance of 1/500. These demands rule out simply fixing the structure firmly: the foundations must be able to slide on the seabed and the deck must hang free of the pylons, so that seismic and tectonic movement is absorbed by controlled sliding, swinging and damping rather than resisted by member strength. The governing combination is the design earthquake plus 50% of the tectonic movements. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Relative pier movement” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：若海峽以每年約 12.5 mm 擴張，120 年累積 12.5×120 = 1,500 mm = 1.5 m；與 2 m 容許相對位移相比剩餘 0.5 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: If the strait widens by about 12.5 mm a year, 120 years accumulate 12.5×120 = 1,500 mm = 1.5 m, leaving 0.5 m of the 2 m allowance.","failure":"常見誤解：「抗震設計的最佳做法永遠是把結構做得更強、更固定。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The best seismic design is always to make the structure stronger and more rigidly fixed.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「墩間相對位移」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Relative pier movement”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b012-v13-01-k1","title":"地震、斷層與海峽擴張的設計需求","titleEn":"Design demands from earthquakes, faults and a widening strait","text":"橋址位於構造活躍的科林斯灣，營運單位公開的設計條件包括：地表尖峰加速度 0.48 g、0.2 至 1.0 s 週期的最大譜加速度 1.2 g、回歸期 2,000 年（120 年設計年限內 5% 超越機率），且相鄰橋墩之間須容許任何方向達 2 m 的斷層相對位移，塔的傾斜容許 1/500。這些需求使傳統「把結構牢牢固定」的做法行不通：基礎必須能在海床上滑移，橋面必須與塔分離懸吊，讓地震與構造位移由可控制的滑動、擺動與阻尼吸收，而不是由構件強度硬抗。","textEn":"The site lies in the tectonically active Gulf of Corinth. The operator’s published design criteria include a peak ground acceleration of 0.48 g, maximum spectral acceleration of 1.2 g for periods of 0.2 to 1.0 s, a 2,000-year return period (5% exceedance in the 120-year design life), up to 2 m of fault movement in any direction between adjacent piers and a pylon tilt allowance of 1/500.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]},{"id":"b012-v13-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：抗震設計的最佳做法永遠是把結構做得更強、更固定。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The best seismic design is always to make the structure stronger and more rigidly fixed. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「地震、斷層與海峽擴張的設計需求」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Design demands from earthquakes, faults and a widening strait\" is correct?","options":["抗震設計的最佳做法永遠是把結構做得更強、更固定。","橋址位於構造活躍的科林斯灣，營運單位公開的設計條件包括：地表尖峰加速度 0.48 g、0.2 至 1.0 s 週期的最大譜加速度 1.2 g、回歸期 2,000 年（120 年設計年限內 5% 超越機率），且相鄰橋墩之間須容許任何方向達 2 m 的斷層相對位移，塔的傾斜容許 1/500。","橋面懸吊在塔上自由擺動，地震時就不需要任何阻尼裝置。"],"optionsEn":["The best seismic design is always to make the structure stronger and more rigidly fixed.","The site lies in the tectonically active Gulf of Corinth.","If the deck hangs freely from the pylons, it needs no damping devices in an earthquake."],"answer":1,"explanation":"橋址位於構造活躍的科林斯灣，營運單位公開的設計條件包括：地表尖峰加速度 0.48 g、0.2 至 1.0 s 週期的最大譜加速度 1.2 g、回歸期 2,000 年（120 年設計年限內 5% 超越機率），且相鄰橋墩之間須容許任何方向達 2 m 的斷層相對位移，塔的傾斜容許 1/500。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The site lies in the tectonically active Gulf of Corinth. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b012-v13-02","title":"地震、斷層與海峽擴張的設計需求：定量估算","titleEn":"Design demands from earthquakes, faults and a widening strait: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"],"prerequisiteIds":["b012-v13-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「墩間相對位移」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Relative pier movement” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：若海峽以每年約 12.5 mm 擴張，120 年累積 12.5×120 = 1,500 mm = 1.5 m；與 2 m 容許相對位移相比剩餘 0.5 m。若擴張速率取 15 mm/年，累積 1.8 m，餘裕只剩 0.2 m，說明構造位移與地震位移需一併規劃。擴張速率為教學假設，2 m 為公開設計值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: If the strait widens by about 12.5 mm a year, 120 years accumulate 12.5×120 = 1,500 mm = 1.5 m, leaving 0.5 m of the 2 m allowance. At 15 mm a year the total is 1.8 m with only 0.2 m to spare, showing that tectonic and seismic displacements must be planned together. The widening rate is a teaching assumption; 2 m is the published design value. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以場址特定地震危害分析建立設計譜與時間歷程，進行含基礎滑移與橋面擺動的非線性時間歷程分析；以岸邊與墩位的測地網定期量測實際構造位移，與設計假設的速率比較，必要時更新剩餘容量評估。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Build design spectra and time histories from a site-specific seismic hazard analysis and run nonlinear time-history analyses including foundation sliding and deck swinging; measure actual tectonic movement periodically with a geodetic network on the shores and at the piers, compare with the assumed rate and update the remaining-capacity assessment when needed.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b012-v13-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"若海峽以每年約 12.5 mm 擴張，120 年累積 12.5×120 = 1,500 mm = 1.5 m；與 2 m 容許相對位移相比剩餘 0.5 m。若擴張速率取 15 mm/年，累積 1.8 m，餘裕只剩 0.2 m，說明構造位移與地震位移需一併規劃。擴張速率為教學假設，2 m 為公開設計值。","textEn":"If the strait widens by about 12.5 mm a year, 120 years accumulate 12.5×120 = 1,500 mm = 1.5 m, leaving 0.5 m of the 2 m allowance. At 15 mm a year the total is 1.8 m with only 0.2 m to spare, showing that tectonic and seismic displacements must be planned together. The widening rate is a teaching assumption; 2 m is the published design value.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]},{"id":"b012-v13-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「地震、斷層與海峽擴張的設計需求」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Design demands from earthquakes, faults and a widening strait\", which statement holds?","options":["混凝土結構太重，不可能在海上浮運。","平衡懸臂只要最後兩側長度相同，中間的施工順序不重要。","若海峽以每年約 12.5 mm 擴張，120 年累積 12.5×120 = 1,500 mm = 1.5 m；與 2 m 容許相對位移相比剩餘 0.5 m。"],"optionsEn":["Concrete structures are too heavy to float and tow at sea.","In balanced cantilever erection only the final equal lengths matter, not the order in between.","If the strait widens by about 12.5 mm a year, 120 years accumulate 12.5×120 = 1,500 mm = 1.5 m, leaving 0.5 m of the 2 m allowance."],"answer":2,"explanation":"若海峽以每年約 12.5 mm 擴張，120 年累積 12.5×120 = 1,500 mm = 1.5 m；與 2 m 容許相對位移相比剩餘 0.5 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"If the strait widens by about 12.5 mm a year, 120 years accumulate 12.5×120 = 1,500 mm = 1.5 m, leaving 0.5 m of the 2 m allowance. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b012-v13-03","title":"地震、斷層與海峽擴張的設計需求：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Design demands from earthquakes, faults and a widening strait: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"],"prerequisiteIds":["b012-v13-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「墩間相對位移」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Relative pier movement” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以場址特定地震危害分析建立設計譜與時間歷程，進行含基礎滑移與橋面擺動的非線性時間歷程分析；以岸邊與墩位的測地網定期量測實際構造位移，與設計假設的速率比較，必要時更新剩餘容量評估。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Build design spectra and time histories from a site-specific seismic hazard analysis and run nonlinear time-history analyses including foundation sliding and deck swinging; measure actual tectonic movement periodically with a geodetic network on the shores and at the piers, compare with the assumed rate and update the remaining-capacity assessment when needed. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：設計基準文件要同時列出地震、構造位移、溫度與風的位移需求，並以「位移預算」逐項分配給基礎滑移、阻尼器行程、伸縮縫與支承；任何預算超支都需設計者書面確認。","observationEn":"Site practice: The design basis should list displacement demands from earthquake, tectonic movement, temperature and wind together and allocate them in a displacement budget to foundation sliding, damper stroke, joints and bearings; any overrun requires the designer’s written confirmation.","failure":"注意干擾：若把基礎嵌固、橋面固定在塔上，地震力會直接灌入塔與基礎，構造位移則在固定點累積成巨大的強迫應力；相鄰墩的相對位移若超過伸縮縫與阻尼器行程，橋面可能撞擊或脫落。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Fixing the foundations and tying the deck to the pylons would drive seismic force straight into pylons and footings while tectonic movement accumulated as huge locked-in stresses; relative pier movement beyond joint and damper travel could make the deck collide or unseat. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b012-v13-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以場址特定地震危害分析建立設計譜與時間歷程，進行含基礎滑移與橋面擺動的非線性時間歷程分析；以岸邊與墩位的測地網定期量測實際構造位移，與設計假設的速率比較，必要時更新剩餘容量評估。","textEn":"Build design spectra and time histories from a site-specific seismic hazard analysis and run nonlinear time-history analyses including foundation sliding and deck swinging; measure actual tectonic movement periodically with a geodetic network on the shores and at the piers, compare with the assumed rate and update the remaining-capacity assessment when needed.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]},{"id":"b012-v13-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"設計基準文件要同時列出地震、構造位移、溫度與風的位移需求，並以「位移預算」逐項分配給基礎滑移、阻尼器行程、伸縮縫與支承；任何預算超支都需設計者書面確認。","textEn":"The design basis should list displacement demands from earthquake, tectonic movement, temperature and wind together and allocate them in a displacement budget to foundation sliding, damper stroke, joints and bearings; any overrun requires the designer’s written confirmation.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「地震、斷層與海峽擴張的設計需求」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Design demands from earthquakes, faults and a widening strait\"?","options":["以場址特定地震危害分析建立設計譜與時間歷程，進行含基礎滑移與橋面擺動的非線性時間歷程分析。","量測時不必記錄溫度、日照、風與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","有了即時感測器，就不需要定期做傳統測量。"],"optionsEn":["Build design spectra and time histories from a site-specific seismic hazard analysis and run nonlinear time-history analyses including foundation sliding and deck swinging.","Temperature, sunshine, wind and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","With real-time sensors there is no need for periodic conventional surveys."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以場址特定地震危害分析建立設計譜與時間歷程，進行含基礎滑移與橋面擺動的非線性時間歷程分析；以岸邊與墩位的測地網定期量測實際構造位移，與設計假設的速率比較，必要時更新剩餘容量評估。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Build design spectra and time histories from a site-specific seismic hazard analysis and run nonlinear time-history analyses including foundation sliding and deck swinging; measure actual tectonic movement periodically with a geodetic network on the shores and at the piers, compare with the assumed rate and update the remaining-capacity assessment when needed. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b012-v13-04","title":"地震、斷層與海峽擴張的設計需求：失效診斷","titleEn":"Design demands from earthquakes, faults and a widening strait: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"],"prerequisiteIds":["b012-v13-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「墩間相對位移」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Relative pier movement” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若把基礎嵌固、橋面固定在塔上，地震力會直接灌入塔與基礎，構造位移則在固定點累積成巨大的強迫應力；相鄰墩的相對位移若超過伸縮縫與阻尼器行程，橋面可能撞擊或脫落。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Fixing the foundations and tying the deck to the pylons would drive seismic force straight into pylons and footings while tectonic movement accumulated as huge locked-in stresses; relative pier movement beyond joint and damper travel could make the deck collide or unseat. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：最不利的設計組合是設計地震加上 50% 的構造位移。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The governing combination is the design earthquake plus 50% of the tectonic movements.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「抗震設計的最佳做法永遠是把結構做得更強、更固定。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The best seismic design is always to make the structure stronger and more rigidly fixed.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b012-v13-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若把基礎嵌固、橋面固定在塔上，地震力會直接灌入塔與基礎，構造位移則在固定點累積成巨大的強迫應力；相鄰墩的相對位移若超過伸縮縫與阻尼器行程，橋面可能撞擊或脫落。","textEn":"Fixing the foundations and tying the deck to the pylons would drive seismic force straight into pylons and footings while tectonic movement accumulated as huge locked-in stresses; relative pier movement beyond joint and damper travel could make the deck collide or unseat.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]},{"id":"b012-v13-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「地震、斷層與海峽擴張的設計需求」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Design demands from earthquakes, faults and a widening strait\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","若把基礎嵌固、橋面固定在塔上，地震力會直接灌入塔與基礎，構造位移則在固定點累積成巨大的強迫應力；相鄰墩的相對位移若超過伸縮縫與阻尼器行程，橋面可能撞擊或脫落。","橋面懸吊在塔上自由擺動，地震時就不需要任何阻尼裝置。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Fixing the foundations and tying the deck to the pylons would drive seismic force straight into pylons and footings while tectonic movement accumulated as huge locked-in stresses.","If the deck hangs freely from the pylons, it needs no damping devices in an earthquake."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若把基礎嵌固、橋面固定在塔上，地震力會直接灌入塔與基礎，構造位移則在固定點累積成巨大的強迫應力；相鄰墩的相對位移若超過伸縮縫與阻尼器行程，橋面可能撞擊或脫落。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Fixing the foundations and tying the deck to the pylons would drive seismic force straight into pylons and footings while tectonic movement accumulated as huge locked-in stresses; relative pier movement beyond joint and damper travel could make the deck collide or unseat. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b012-v13-05","title":"連續全懸吊橋面：熔斷限制器與黏滯阻尼器：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Continuous suspended deck: fuse restrainers and viscous dampers: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"],"prerequisiteIds":["b012-v13-04"],"objective":"說明「熔斷限制器」如何影響里翁—安提里翁大橋的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Fuse restrainers” governs force, deformation or durability in “Rion–Antirion Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"里翁—安提里翁大橋的橋面在全長 2,252 m 連續，並完全由斜索懸吊，不直接坐在塔上，地震時橋面像巨大的擺錘相對塔擺動。營運單位公開的配置是：主墩設 10.5 MN、過渡墩設 3.5 MN 的熔斷限制器，平時在強風下把橋面固定，地震時降伏斷開；同時並聯每支 3.5 MN 的黏滯阻尼器，塔位 4 支、過渡墩 2 支，主墩行程 −1,650 至 +1,850 mm，過渡墩 ±2,600 mm。熔斷限制器提供常時剛度，阻尼器在熔斷後限制擺幅並消耗能量，兩者分工讓風與地震的需求不必用同一個元件妥協。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「熔斷限制器」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The Rion–Antirion deck is continuous over its full 2,252 m and fully suspended by stays rather than resting on the pylons, so in an earthquake it swings like a giant pendulum relative to them. The operator’s published layout has fuse restrainers of 10.5 MN at the main piers and 3.5 MN at the transition piers that hold the deck in strong wind and yield in an earthquake, in parallel with viscous dampers of 3.5 MN each, 4 at the pylons and 2 at the transition piers, with strokes of −1,650 to +1,850 mm at main piers and ±2,600 mm at transition piers. The fuses provide everyday stiffness and the dampers limit swing and dissipate energy after the fuses break, so wind and seismic demands need not be compromised in one device. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Fuse restrainers” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：阻尼力 F = C·v^α，取 α = 0.15、在 v = 1.6 m/s 時 F = 3,500 kN：C = 3,500/1.6^0.15 ≈ 3,262 kN/(m/s)^0.15；v = 0.1 m/s 時 F ≈ 3,262×0.708 ≈ 2,309 kN，速度降為 1/16 力只降約 34%。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Damper force F = C·v^α; with α = 0.15 and F = 3,500 kN at v = 1.6 m/s, C = 3,500/1.6^0.15 ≈ 3,262 kN/(m/s)^0.15, and at v = 0.1 m/s F ≈ 3,262×0.708 ≈ 2,309 kN: a sixteen-fold drop in speed lowers force by only about 34%.","failure":"常見誤解：「橋面懸吊在塔上自由擺動，地震時就不需要任何阻尼裝置。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"If the deck hangs freely from the pylons, it needs no damping devices in an earthquake.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「熔斷限制器」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Fuse restrainers”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b012-v13-05-k1","title":"連續全懸吊橋面：熔斷限制器與黏滯阻尼器","titleEn":"Continuous suspended deck: fuse restrainers and viscous dampers","text":"里翁—安提里翁大橋的橋面在全長 2,252 m 連續，並完全由斜索懸吊，不直接坐在塔上，地震時橋面像巨大的擺錘相對塔擺動。營運單位公開的配置是：主墩設 10.5 MN、過渡墩設 3.5 MN 的熔斷限制器，平時在強風下把橋面固定，地震時降伏斷開；同時並聯每支 3.5 MN 的黏滯阻尼器，塔位 4 支、過渡墩 2 支，主墩行程 −1,650 至 +1,850 mm，過渡墩 ±2,600 mm。","textEn":"The Rion–Antirion deck is continuous over its full 2,252 m and fully suspended by stays rather than resting on the pylons, so in an earthquake it swings like a giant pendulum relative to them. The operator’s published layout has fuse restrainers of 10.5 MN at the main piers and 3.5 MN at the transition piers that hold the deck in strong wind and yield in an earthquake, in parallel with viscous dampers of 3.5 MN each, 4 at the pylons and 2 at the transition piers, with strokes of −1,650 to +1,850 mm at main piers and ±2,600 mm at transition piers.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]},{"id":"b012-v13-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：橋面懸吊在塔上自由擺動，地震時就不需要任何阻尼裝置。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: If the deck hangs freely from the pylons, it needs no damping devices in an earthquake. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「連續全懸吊橋面：熔斷限制器與黏滯阻尼器」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Continuous suspended deck: fuse restrainers and viscous dampers\" is correct?","options":["橋面懸吊在塔上自由擺動，地震時就不需要任何阻尼裝置。","軟弱海床上的大橋基礎一定要用長樁打到岩盤。","里翁—安提里翁大橋的橋面在全長 2,252 m 連續，並完全由斜索懸吊，不直接坐在塔上，地震時橋面像巨大的擺錘相對塔擺動。"],"optionsEn":["If the deck hangs freely from the pylons, it needs no damping devices in an earthquake.","Bridge foundations on soft seabed must always use long piles driven to rock.","The Rion–Antirion deck is continuous over its full 2,252 m and fully suspended by stays rather than resting on the pylons, so in an earthquake it swings like a giant pendulum relative to them."],"answer":2,"explanation":"里翁—安提里翁大橋的橋面在全長 2,252 m 連續，並完全由斜索懸吊，不直接坐在塔上，地震時橋面像巨大的擺錘相對塔擺動。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The Rion–Antirion deck is continuous over its full 2,252 m and fully suspended by stays rather than resting on the pylons, so in an earthquake it swings like a giant pendulum relative to them. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b012-v13-06","title":"連續全懸吊橋面：熔斷限制器與黏滯阻尼器：定量估算","titleEn":"Continuous suspended deck: fuse restrainers and viscous dampers: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"],"prerequisiteIds":["b012-v13-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「熔斷限制器」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Fuse restrainers” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：阻尼力 F = C·v^α，取 α = 0.15、在 v = 1.6 m/s 時 F = 3,500 kN：C = 3,500/1.6^0.15 ≈ 3,262 kN/(m/s)^0.15；v = 0.1 m/s 時 F ≈ 3,262×0.708 ≈ 2,309 kN，速度降為 1/16 力只降約 34%。主墩熔斷力 10.5 MN 是單支阻尼器容量的 3 倍。α 與速度為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Damper force F = C·v^α; with α = 0.15 and F = 3,500 kN at v = 1.6 m/s, C = 3,500/1.6^0.15 ≈ 3,262 kN/(m/s)^0.15, and at v = 0.1 m/s F ≈ 3,262×0.708 ≈ 2,309 kN: a sixteen-fold drop in speed lowers force by only about 34%. The 10.5 MN main-pier fuse is 3 times one damper’s capacity. α and velocities are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：熔斷元件以抽樣破壞試驗確認斷開力在設計範圍內，阻尼器做全尺寸力—速度與行程試驗；營運期以限制器上的荷重計長期記錄風力與溫度造成的力，確認遠低於熔斷值；地震後依荷重計資料判斷是否需要更換熔斷元件並重新校準。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Confirm fuse break force by sample destructive tests and test dampers full-size for force–velocity and stroke; in service record wind- and temperature-induced forces on the restrainer load cells to confirm they stay well below the fuse value, and after an earthquake use the load-cell data to decide whether fuses must be replaced and recalibrated.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b012-v13-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"阻尼力 F = C·v^α，取 α = 0.15、在 v = 1.6 m/s 時 F = 3,500 kN：C = 3,500/1.6^0.15 ≈ 3,262 kN/(m/s)^0.15；v = 0.1 m/s 時 F ≈ 3,262×0.708 ≈ 2,309 kN，速度降為 1/16 力只降約 34%。主墩熔斷力 10.5 MN 是單支阻尼器容量的 3 倍。α 與速度為教學假設。","textEn":"Damper force F = C·v^α; with α = 0.15 and F = 3,500 kN at v = 1.6 m/s, C = 3,500/1.6^0.15 ≈ 3,262 kN/(m/s)^0.15, and at v = 0.1 m/s F ≈ 3,262×0.708 ≈ 2,309 kN: a sixteen-fold drop in speed lowers force by only about 34%. The 10.5 MN main-pier fuse is 3 times one damper’s capacity. α and velocities are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]},{"id":"b012-v13-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「連續全懸吊橋面：熔斷限制器與黏滯阻尼器」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Continuous suspended deck: fuse restrainers and viscous dampers\", which statement holds?","options":["阻尼力 F = C·v^α，取 α = 0.15、在 v = 1.6 m/s 時 F = 3,500 kN：C = 3,500/1.6^0.15 ≈ 3,262 kN/(m/s)^0.15。","深海的礫石墊層只是填料，平整度要求可以放寬。","感測器越多、取樣越快，監測系統就一定越有用。"],"optionsEn":["Damper force F = C·v^α.","A deep-water gravel bed is just fill, so its flatness can be relaxed.","More sensors and faster sampling always make a monitoring system more useful."],"answer":0,"explanation":"阻尼力 F = C·v^α，取 α = 0.15、在 v = 1.6 m/s 時 F = 3,500 kN：C = 3,500/1.6^0.15 ≈ 3,262 kN/(m/s)^0.15；v = 0.1 m/s 時 F ≈ 3,262×0.708 ≈ 2,309 kN，速度降為 1/16 力只降約 34%。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Damper force F = C·v^α; with α = 0.15 and F = 3,500 kN at v = 1.6 m/s, C = 3,500/1.6^0.15 ≈ 3,262 kN/(m/s)^0.15, and at v = 0.1 m/s F ≈ 3,262×0.708 ≈ 2,309 kN: a sixteen-fold drop in speed lowers force by only about 34%. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b012-v13-07","title":"連續全懸吊橋面：熔斷限制器與黏滯阻尼器：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Continuous suspended deck: fuse restrainers and viscous dampers: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"],"prerequisiteIds":["b012-v13-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「熔斷限制器」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Fuse restrainers” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"熔斷元件以抽樣破壞試驗確認斷開力在設計範圍內，阻尼器做全尺寸力—速度與行程試驗；營運期以限制器上的荷重計長期記錄風力與溫度造成的力，確認遠低於熔斷值；地震後依荷重計資料判斷是否需要更換熔斷元件並重新校準。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Confirm fuse break force by sample destructive tests and test dampers full-size for force–velocity and stroke; in service record wind- and temperature-induced forces on the restrainer load cells to confirm they stay well below the fuse value, and after an earthquake use the load-cell data to decide whether fuses must be replaced and recalibrated. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：熔斷元件應設計為地震後可快速更換的消耗件，並在現場或倉庫保留備品；監測系統要把限制器荷重與阻尼器行程列為事件後自動報告的必要內容。","observationEn":"Site practice: Design fuses as sacrificial parts that can be replaced quickly after an earthquake, keep spares on site or in store, and make restrainer loads and damper strokes mandatory content of automatic post-event reports.","failure":"注意干擾：熔斷值設得太低，強風或溫度力就會讓限制器斷開，橋面在日常風中擺動；設得太高，地震時不斷開，巨大的慣性力經限制器傳到塔與基礎。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A fuse set too low breaks in strong wind or under temperature force and lets the deck swing in everyday wind; set too high it does not break in an earthquake and sends huge inertia forces through to the pylons and foundations; insufficient damper stroke can hit the end stops late in a major quake. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b012-v13-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"熔斷元件以抽樣破壞試驗確認斷開力在設計範圍內，阻尼器做全尺寸力—速度與行程試驗；營運期以限制器上的荷重計長期記錄風力與溫度造成的力，確認遠低於熔斷值；地震後依荷重計資料判斷是否需要更換熔斷元件並重新校準。","textEn":"Confirm fuse break force by sample destructive tests and test dampers full-size for force–velocity and stroke; in service record wind- and temperature-induced forces on the restrainer load cells to confirm they stay well below the fuse value, and after an earthquake use the load-cell data to decide whether fuses must be replaced and recalibrated.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]},{"id":"b012-v13-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"熔斷元件應設計為地震後可快速更換的消耗件，並在現場或倉庫保留備品；監測系統要把限制器荷重與阻尼器行程列為事件後自動報告的必要內容。","textEn":"Design fuses as sacrificial parts that can be replaced quickly after an earthquake, keep spares on site or in store, and make restrainer loads and damper strokes mandatory content of automatic post-event reports.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「連續全懸吊橋面：熔斷限制器與黏滯阻尼器」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Continuous suspended deck: fuse restrainers and viscous dampers\"?","options":["沿用另一座橋或另一棟建築的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","熔斷元件以抽樣破壞試驗確認斷開力在設計範圍內，阻尼器做全尺寸力—速度與行程試驗。","斜索是由許多鋼絞線組成的，所以整根斜索不可能突然失效。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another bridge or building counts as verifying this structure.","Confirm fuse break force by sample destructive tests and test dampers full-size for force–velocity and stroke.","Because a stay is made of many strands, the whole stay can never fail suddenly."],"answer":1,"explanation":"熔斷元件以抽樣破壞試驗確認斷開力在設計範圍內，阻尼器做全尺寸力—速度與行程試驗；營運期以限制器上的荷重計長期記錄風力與溫度造成的力，確認遠低於熔斷值；地震後依荷重計資料判斷是否需要更換熔斷元件並重新校準。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Confirm fuse break force by sample destructive tests and test dampers full-size for force–velocity and stroke; in service record wind- and temperature-induced forces on the restrainer load cells to confirm they stay well below the fuse value, and after an earthquake use the load-cell data to decide whether fuses must be replaced and recalibrated. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b012-v13-08","title":"連續全懸吊橋面：熔斷限制器與黏滯阻尼器：失效診斷","titleEn":"Continuous suspended deck: fuse restrainers and viscous dampers: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"],"prerequisiteIds":["b012-v13-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「熔斷限制器」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Fuse restrainers” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"熔斷值設得太低，強風或溫度力就會讓限制器斷開，橋面在日常風中擺動；設得太高，地震時不斷開，巨大的慣性力經限制器傳到塔與基礎。阻尼器行程不足則可能在大地震末段撞擊止擋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A fuse set too low breaks in strong wind or under temperature force and lets the deck swing in everyday wind; set too high it does not break in an earthquake and sends huge inertia forces through to the pylons and foundations; insufficient damper stroke can hit the end stops late in a major quake. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：熔斷限制器提供常時剛度，阻尼器在熔斷後限制擺幅並消耗能量，兩者分工讓風與地震的需求不必用同一個元件妥協。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The fuses provide everyday stiffness and the dampers limit swing and dissipate energy after the fuses break, so wind and seismic demands need not be compromised in one device.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「橋面懸吊在塔上自由擺動，地震時就不需要任何阻尼裝置。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"If the deck hangs freely from the pylons, it needs no damping devices in an earthquake.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b012-v13-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"熔斷值設得太低，強風或溫度力就會讓限制器斷開，橋面在日常風中擺動；設得太高，地震時不斷開，巨大的慣性力經限制器傳到塔與基礎。阻尼器行程不足則可能在大地震末段撞擊止擋。","textEn":"A fuse set too low breaks in strong wind or under temperature force and lets the deck swing in everyday wind; set too high it does not break in an earthquake and sends huge inertia forces through to the pylons and foundations; insufficient damper stroke can hit the end stops late in a major quake.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]},{"id":"b012-v13-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「連續全懸吊橋面：熔斷限制器與黏滯阻尼器」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Continuous suspended deck: fuse restrainers and viscous dampers\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","軟弱海床上的大橋基礎一定要用長樁打到岩盤。","熔斷值設得太低，強風或溫度力就會讓限制器斷開，橋面在日常風中擺動；設得太高，地震時不斷開，巨大的慣性力經限制器傳到塔與基礎。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Bridge foundations on soft seabed must always use long piles driven to rock.","A fuse set too low breaks in strong wind or under temperature force and lets the deck swing in everyday wind."],"answer":2,"explanation":"熔斷值設得太低，強風或溫度力就會讓限制器斷開，橋面在日常風中擺動；設得太高，地震時不斷開，巨大的慣性力經限制器傳到塔與基礎。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A fuse set too low breaks in strong wind or under temperature force and lets the deck swing in everyday wind; set too high it does not break in an earthquake and sends huge inertia forces through to the pylons and foundations; insufficient damper stroke can hit the end stops late in a major quake. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b012-v13-s2","title":"材料、構件與接合細部","titleEn":"Materials, members and connection details","description":"本階段聚焦「加勁土壤與可滑移基礎」與「90 m 沉箱的乾塢製作與浮運」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Reinforced soil and sliding foundations\" and \"Dry-dock casting and floating of the 90 m caissons\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b012-v13-09","title":"加勁土壤與可滑移基礎：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Reinforced soil and sliding foundations: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"],"prerequisiteIds":["b012-v13-08"],"objective":"說明「鋼管插入物」如何影響里翁—安提里翁大橋的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Steel-pipe inclusions” governs force, deformation or durability in “Rion–Antirion Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"海床沉積層厚度超過 500 m，以黏土為主夾砂與粉土，調查至海床下 100 m 仍未見岩盤，打樁到岩盤不可行。營運單位公開資料指出，設計在每座墩下打入約 150 至 200 根直徑 2 m、長 25 至 30 m、間距 7 m 的中空鋼管，改良上部 20 m 土層，再鋪 3 m 厚礫石層，基礎直接坐在礫石上而不與鋼管連接。鋼管提高土壤的剪力強度與承載，避免基礎傾覆或大量沉陷；礫石層則讓基礎在強震時可以水平滑移，限制傳入上部結構的力量，這是「容量設計」觀念在基礎上的應用。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「鋼管插入物」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The seabed sediments are over 500 m thick, mainly clay with sand and silt, and no rock was found within 100 m below the seabed, so piling to rock was not possible. Operator data state that about 150 to 200 hollow steel pipes, 2 m in diameter, 25 to 30 m long and 7 m apart, were driven under each pier to improve the top 20 m of soil, then a 3 m gravel layer was placed and the footing rests on the gravel without connection to the pipes. The inclusions raise the soil’s shear strength and bearing to prevent overturning or large settlement, while the gravel lets the footing slide horizontally in a strong earthquake, capping the force transmitted to the superstructure: capacity design applied to a foundation. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Steel-pipe inclusions” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：面積置換率 a_s = π·r²/s² = π×1²/7² ≈ 6.4%。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Area replacement ratio a_s = π·r²/s² = π×1²/7² ≈ 6.4%.","failure":"常見誤解：「軟弱海床上的大橋基礎一定要用長樁打到岩盤。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Bridge foundations on soft seabed must always use long piles driven to rock.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「鋼管插入物」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Steel-pipe inclusions”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b012-v13-09-k1","title":"加勁土壤與可滑移基礎","titleEn":"Reinforced soil and sliding foundations","text":"海床沉積層厚度超過 500 m，以黏土為主夾砂與粉土，調查至海床下 100 m 仍未見岩盤，打樁到岩盤不可行。營運單位公開資料指出，設計在每座墩下打入約 150 至 200 根直徑 2 m、長 25 至 30 m、間距 7 m 的中空鋼管，改良上部 20 m 土層，再鋪 3 m 厚礫石層，基礎直接坐在礫石上而不與鋼管連接。","textEn":"The seabed sediments are over 500 m thick, mainly clay with sand and silt, and no rock was found within 100 m below the seabed, so piling to rock was not possible. Operator data state that about 150 to 200 hollow steel pipes, 2 m in diameter, 25 to 30 m long and 7 m apart, were driven under each pier to improve the top 20 m of soil, then a 3 m gravel layer was placed and the footing rests on the gravel without connection to the pipes.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]},{"id":"b012-v13-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：軟弱海床上的大橋基礎一定要用長樁打到岩盤。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Bridge foundations on soft seabed must always use long piles driven to rock. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「加勁土壤與可滑移基礎」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Reinforced soil and sliding foundations\" is correct?","options":["海床沉積層厚度超過 500 m，以黏土為主夾砂與粉土，調查至海床下 100 m 仍未見岩盤，打樁到岩盤不可行。","軟弱海床上的大橋基礎一定要用長樁打到岩盤。","混凝土結構太重，不可能在海上浮運。"],"optionsEn":["The seabed sediments are over 500 m thick, mainly clay with sand and silt, and no rock was found within 100 m below the seabed, so piling to rock was not possible.","Bridge foundations on soft seabed must always use long piles driven to rock.","Concrete structures are too heavy to float and tow at sea."],"answer":0,"explanation":"海床沉積層厚度超過 500 m，以黏土為主夾砂與粉土，調查至海床下 100 m 仍未見岩盤，打樁到岩盤不可行。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The seabed sediments are over 500 m thick, mainly clay with sand and silt, and no rock was found within 100 m below the seabed, so piling to rock was not possible. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b012-v13-10","title":"加勁土壤與可滑移基礎：定量估算","titleEn":"Reinforced soil and sliding foundations: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"],"prerequisiteIds":["b012-v13-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「鋼管插入物」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Steel-pipe inclusions” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：面積置換率 a_s = π·r²/s² = π×1²/7² ≈ 6.4%。基礎滑移前可傳遞的最大水平力 H = N·tanφ：取有效垂直力 N = 600,000 kN、礫石摩擦角 φ = 35°（tanφ ≈ 0.700），H ≈ 420,000 kN；超過此值基礎滑移，上部力量不再增加。N 與 φ 為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Area replacement ratio a_s = π·r²/s² = π×1²/7² ≈ 6.4%. The largest horizontal force before the footing slides is H = N·tanφ; with an effective vertical force N = 600,000 kN and gravel friction angle φ = 35° (tanφ ≈ 0.700), H ≈ 420,000 kN, beyond which the footing slides and the force on the superstructure stops rising. N and φ are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以離心機模型或數值分析驗證加勁土壤在反覆荷載下的承載與滑移行為；施工時逐根記錄插入物的貫入深度與位置，礫石層以水下測深確認厚度與平整度；營運期以測地與沉陷量測確認基礎沉陷落在預期的 0.1 至 0.2 m 範圍。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Verify the bearing and sliding behaviour of the reinforced soil under cyclic loading with centrifuge models or numerical analysis; record each inclusion’s penetration and position during construction and confirm gravel thickness and flatness by underwater survey; in service confirm footing settlement stays within the expected 0.1 to 0.2 m by geodetic and settlement measurements.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b012-v13-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"面積置換率 a_s = π·r²/s² = π×1²/7² ≈ 6.4%。基礎滑移前可傳遞的最大水平力 H = N·tanφ：取有效垂直力 N = 600,000 kN、礫石摩擦角 φ = 35°（tanφ ≈ 0.700），H ≈ 420,000 kN；超過此值基礎滑移，上部力量不再增加。N 與 φ 為教學假設。","textEn":"Area replacement ratio a_s = π·r²/s² = π×1²/7² ≈ 6.4%. The largest horizontal force before the footing slides is H = N·tanφ; with an effective vertical force N = 600,000 kN and gravel friction angle φ = 35° (tanφ ≈ 0.700), H ≈ 420,000 kN, beyond which the footing slides and the force on the superstructure stops rising. N and φ are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]},{"id":"b012-v13-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「加勁土壤與可滑移基礎」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Reinforced soil and sliding foundations\", which statement holds?","options":["平衡懸臂只要最後兩側長度相同，中間的施工順序不重要。","面積置換率 a_s = π·r²/s² = π×1²/7² ≈ 6.4%。","有了即時感測器，就不需要定期做傳統測量。"],"optionsEn":["In balanced cantilever erection only the final equal lengths matter, not the order in between.","Area replacement ratio a_s = π·r²/s² = π×1²/7² ≈ 6.4%.","With real-time sensors there is no need for periodic conventional surveys."],"answer":1,"explanation":"面積置換率 a_s = π·r²/s² = π×1²/7² ≈ 6.4%。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Area replacement ratio a_s = π·r²/s² = π×1²/7² ≈ 6.4%. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b012-v13-11","title":"加勁土壤與可滑移基礎：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Reinforced soil and sliding foundations: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"],"prerequisiteIds":["b012-v13-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「鋼管插入物」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Steel-pipe inclusions” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以離心機模型或數值分析驗證加勁土壤在反覆荷載下的承載與滑移行為；施工時逐根記錄插入物的貫入深度與位置，礫石層以水下測深確認厚度與平整度；營運期以測地與沉陷量測確認基礎沉陷落在預期的 0.1 至 0.2 m 範圍。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Verify the bearing and sliding behaviour of the reinforced soil under cyclic loading with centrifuge models or numerical analysis; record each inclusion’s penetration and position during construction and confirm gravel thickness and flatness by underwater survey; in service confirm footing settlement stays within the expected 0.1 to 0.2 m by geodetic and settlement measurements. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：基礎設計報告要清楚區分「加勁土壤」與「樁基礎」的力學假設，並在圖上註明礫石層與基礎之間不得有任何連接；水下施工記錄（插入物位置、礫石厚度）要完整交接給營運單位。","observationEn":"Site practice: The foundation report must clearly separate the mechanics of reinforced soil from piled foundations and the drawings must state that nothing connects the footing to the gravel; underwater construction records of inclusion positions and gravel thickness must be handed over completely to the operator.","failure":"注意干擾：若把插入物當成樁並與基礎剛接，地震時樁頭承受巨大剪力與彎矩，可能破壞；礫石層摩擦過高則基礎不滑移，上部結構承受遠超預期的地震力；插入物不足則基礎可能傾覆或產生不均勻沉陷。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Treating the inclusions as piles rigidly tied to the footing would load their heads with huge shear and moment in an earthquake; gravel friction that is too high prevents sliding and exposes the superstructure to far larger forces; too few inclusions risk overturning or differential settlement. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b012-v13-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以離心機模型或數值分析驗證加勁土壤在反覆荷載下的承載與滑移行為；施工時逐根記錄插入物的貫入深度與位置，礫石層以水下測深確認厚度與平整度；營運期以測地與沉陷量測確認基礎沉陷落在預期的 0.1 至 0.2 m 範圍。","textEn":"Verify the bearing and sliding behaviour of the reinforced soil under cyclic loading with centrifuge models or numerical analysis; record each inclusion’s penetration and position during construction and confirm gravel thickness and flatness by underwater survey; in service confirm footing settlement stays within the expected 0.1 to 0.2 m by geodetic and settlement measurements.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]},{"id":"b012-v13-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"基礎設計報告要清楚區分「加勁土壤」與「樁基礎」的力學假設，並在圖上註明礫石層與基礎之間不得有任何連接；水下施工記錄（插入物位置、礫石厚度）要完整交接給營運單位。","textEn":"The foundation report must clearly separate the mechanics of reinforced soil from piled foundations and the drawings must state that nothing connects the footing to the gravel; underwater construction records of inclusion positions and gravel thickness must be handed over completely to the operator.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「加勁土壤與可滑移基礎」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Reinforced soil and sliding foundations\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","高強度海工混凝土在 120 年內不需要任何耐久性檢測。","以離心機模型或數值分析驗證加勁土壤在反覆荷載下的承載與滑移行為。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","High-strength marine concrete needs no durability testing over 120 years.","Verify the bearing and sliding behaviour of the reinforced soil under cyclic loading with centrifuge models or numerical analysis."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以離心機模型或數值分析驗證加勁土壤在反覆荷載下的承載與滑移行為；施工時逐根記錄插入物的貫入深度與位置，礫石層以水下測深確認厚度與平整度；營運期以測地與沉陷量測確認基礎沉陷落在預期的 0.1 至 0.2 m 範圍。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Verify the bearing and sliding behaviour of the reinforced soil under cyclic loading with centrifuge models or numerical analysis; record each inclusion’s penetration and position during construction and confirm gravel thickness and flatness by underwater survey; in service confirm footing settlement stays within the expected 0.1 to 0.2 m by geodetic and settlement measurements. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b012-v13-12","title":"加勁土壤與可滑移基礎：失效診斷","titleEn":"Reinforced soil and sliding foundations: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"],"prerequisiteIds":["b012-v13-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「鋼管插入物」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Steel-pipe inclusions” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若把插入物當成樁並與基礎剛接，地震時樁頭承受巨大剪力與彎矩，可能破壞；礫石層摩擦過高則基礎不滑移，上部結構承受遠超預期的地震力；插入物不足則基礎可能傾覆或產生不均勻沉陷。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Treating the inclusions as piles rigidly tied to the footing would load their heads with huge shear and moment in an earthquake; gravel friction that is too high prevents sliding and exposes the superstructure to far larger forces; too few inclusions risk overturning or differential settlement. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：鋼管提高土壤的剪力強度與承載，避免基礎傾覆或大量沉陷；礫石層則讓基礎在強震時可以水平滑移，限制傳入上部結構的力量，這是「容量設計」觀念在基礎上的應用。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The inclusions raise the soil’s shear strength and bearing to prevent overturning or large settlement, while the gravel lets the footing slide horizontally in a strong earthquake, capping the force transmitted to the superstructure: capacity design applied to a foundation.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「軟弱海床上的大橋基礎一定要用長樁打到岩盤。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Bridge foundations on soft seabed must always use long piles driven to rock.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b012-v13-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若把插入物當成樁並與基礎剛接，地震時樁頭承受巨大剪力與彎矩，可能破壞；礫石層摩擦過高則基礎不滑移，上部結構承受遠超預期的地震力；插入物不足則基礎可能傾覆或產生不均勻沉陷。","textEn":"Treating the inclusions as piles rigidly tied to the footing would load their heads with huge shear and moment in an earthquake; gravel friction that is too high prevents sliding and exposes the superstructure to far larger forces; too few inclusions risk overturning or differential settlement.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]},{"id":"b012-v13-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「加勁土壤與可滑移基礎」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Reinforced soil and sliding foundations\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["若把插入物當成樁並與基礎剛接，地震時樁頭承受巨大剪力與彎矩，可能破壞。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","混凝土結構太重，不可能在海上浮運。"],"optionsEn":["Treating the inclusions as piles rigidly tied to the footing would load their heads with huge shear and moment in an earthquake.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Concrete structures are too heavy to float and tow at sea."],"answer":0,"explanation":"若把插入物當成樁並與基礎剛接，地震時樁頭承受巨大剪力與彎矩，可能破壞；礫石層摩擦過高則基礎不滑移，上部結構承受遠超預期的地震力；插入物不足則基礎可能傾覆或產生不均勻沉陷。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Treating the inclusions as piles rigidly tied to the footing would load their heads with huge shear and moment in an earthquake; gravel friction that is too high prevents sliding and exposes the superstructure to far larger forces; too few inclusions risk overturning or differential settlement. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b012-v13-13","title":"90 m 沉箱的乾塢製作與浮運：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Dry-dock casting and floating of the 90 m caissons: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"],"prerequisiteIds":["b012-v13-12"],"objective":"說明「90 m 直徑基礎」如何影響里翁—安提里翁大橋的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “90 m diameter footings” governs force, deformation or durability in “Rion–Antirion Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"每座塔基礎直徑 90 m，上接由 38 m 漸縮到 26 m 的錐形墩身，再接邊長 38 m、由四支 4 m × 4 m 混凝土腿組成的塔座。營運單位公開資料指出，基礎底部在長 200 m、寬 100 m、深 14 m 的乾塢中製作，可同時做兩座；底部澆到約 15 m 高、具備足夠浮力後灌水浮出，拖到濕塢繼續在浮動狀態下接高錐形段，最後拖到墩位以壓艙水下沉就位。這個方法把大量混凝土作業移到岸邊受控環境，但浮運期間的吃水、穩定性與拖航條件都必須精確計算。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「90 m 直徑基礎」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Each pylon footing is 90 m in diameter, topped by a conical shaft tapering from 38 m to 26 m and a 38 m square pylon base with four 4 m × 4 m concrete legs. Operator data state that the footing bases were cast in a dry dock 200 m long, 100 m wide and 14 m deep, two at a time; once about 15 m high and buoyant, they were floated out, towed to a wet dock where the conical part was built while floating, then towed to position and sunk with ballast water. The method moves most concrete work to a controlled shore site, but draft, stability and towing conditions while afloat must be calculated precisely. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “90 m diameter footings” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：吃水 d = W/(ρ_w·A)。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Draft d = W/(ρ_w·A).","failure":"常見誤解：「混凝土結構太重，不可能在海上浮運。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Concrete structures are too heavy to float and tow at sea.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「90 m 直徑基礎」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “90 m diameter footings”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b012-v13-13-k1","title":"90 m 沉箱的乾塢製作與浮運","titleEn":"Dry-dock casting and floating of the 90 m caissons","text":"每座塔基礎直徑 90 m，上接由 38 m 漸縮到 26 m 的錐形墩身，再接邊長 38 m、由四支 4 m × 4 m 混凝土腿組成的塔座。營運單位公開資料指出，基礎底部在長 200 m、寬 100 m、深 14 m 的乾塢中製作，可同時做兩座；底部澆到約 15 m 高、具備足夠浮力後灌水浮出，拖到濕塢繼續在浮動狀態下接高錐形段，最後拖到墩位以壓艙水下沉就位。","textEn":"Each pylon footing is 90 m in diameter, topped by a conical shaft tapering from 38 m to 26 m and a 38 m square pylon base with four 4 m × 4 m concrete legs. Operator data state that the footing bases were cast in a dry dock 200 m long, 100 m wide and 14 m deep, two at a time; once about 15 m high and buoyant, they were floated out, towed to a wet dock where the conical part was built while floating, then towed to position and sunk with ballast water.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]},{"id":"b012-v13-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：混凝土結構太重，不可能在海上浮運。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Concrete structures are too heavy to float and tow at sea. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「90 m 沉箱的乾塢製作與浮運」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Dry-dock casting and floating of the 90 m caissons\" is correct?","options":["混凝土結構太重，不可能在海上浮運。","每座塔基礎直徑 90 m，上接由 38 m 漸縮到 26 m 的錐形墩身，再接邊長 38 m、由四支 4 m × 4 m 混凝土腿組成的塔座。","深海的礫石墊層只是填料，平整度要求可以放寬。"],"optionsEn":["Concrete structures are too heavy to float and tow at sea.","Each pylon footing is 90 m in diameter, topped by a conical shaft tapering from 38 m to 26 m and a 38 m square pylon base with four 4 m × 4 m concrete legs.","A deep-water gravel bed is just fill, so its flatness can be relaxed."],"answer":1,"explanation":"每座塔基礎直徑 90 m，上接由 38 m 漸縮到 26 m 的錐形墩身，再接邊長 38 m、由四支 4 m × 4 m 混凝土腿組成的塔座。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Each pylon footing is 90 m in diameter, topped by a conical shaft tapering from 38 m to 26 m and a 38 m square pylon base with four 4 m × 4 m concrete legs. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b012-v13-14","title":"90 m 沉箱的乾塢製作與浮運：定量估算","titleEn":"Dry-dock casting and floating of the 90 m caissons: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"],"prerequisiteIds":["b012-v13-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「90 m 直徑基礎」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “90 m diameter footings” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：吃水 d = W/(ρ_w·A)。底面積 A = π×45² ≈ 6,362 m²，每公尺吃水排水約 6,362×1.025 ≈ 6,521 t；若浮出時結構重 60,000 t，d ≈ 60,000/6,521 ≈ 9.2 m，低於乾塢 14 m 深度，留有約 4.8 m 餘裕。重量為教學假設，尺寸為公開資料。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Draft d = W/(ρ_w·A). The base area A = π×45² ≈ 6,362 m² displaces about 6,362×1.025 ≈ 6,521 t per metre of draft; a 60,000 t structure at float-out draws d ≈ 60,000/6,521 ≈ 9.2 m, below the 14 m dock depth with about 4.8 m to spare. The weight is a teaching assumption; dimensions are published values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：每次澆置後以實際混凝土量與密度更新重量與重心，計算吃水、穩心高度與拖航時的傾斜；浮出與下沉作業前確認潮位、波浪與拖船配置，下沉過程以壓艙水量與四周吃水尺同步監控，確保均勻下沉。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: After each pour update weight and centre of gravity from actual quantities and density and compute draft, metacentric height and heel under tow; before float-out and sinking confirm tide, waves and tug arrangement, and during sinking monitor ballast volumes and draft marks around the perimeter to keep the descent level.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b012-v13-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"吃水 d = W/(ρ_w·A)。底面積 A = π×45² ≈ 6,362 m²，每公尺吃水排水約 6,362×1.025 ≈ 6,521 t；若浮出時結構重 60,000 t，d ≈ 60,000/6,521 ≈ 9.2 m，低於乾塢 14 m 深度，留有約 4.8 m 餘裕。重量為教學假設，尺寸為公開資料。","textEn":"Draft d = W/(ρ_w·A). The base area A = π×45² ≈ 6,362 m² displaces about 6,362×1.025 ≈ 6,521 t per metre of draft; a 60,000 t structure at float-out draws d ≈ 60,000/6,521 ≈ 9.2 m, below the 14 m dock depth with about 4.8 m to spare. The weight is a teaching assumption; dimensions are published values.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]},{"id":"b012-v13-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「90 m 沉箱的乾塢製作與浮運」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Dry-dock casting and floating of the 90 m caissons\", which statement holds?","options":["感測器越多、取樣越快，監測系統就一定越有用。","斜索是由許多鋼絞線組成的，所以整根斜索不可能突然失效。","吃水 d = W/(ρ_w·A)。"],"optionsEn":["More sensors and faster sampling always make a monitoring system more useful.","Because a stay is made of many strands, the whole stay can never fail suddenly.","Draft d = W/(ρ_w·A)."],"answer":2,"explanation":"吃水 d = W/(ρ_w·A)。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Draft d = W/(ρ_w·A). Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b012-v13-15","title":"90 m 沉箱的乾塢製作與浮運：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Dry-dock casting and floating of the 90 m caissons: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"],"prerequisiteIds":["b012-v13-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「90 m 直徑基礎」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “90 m diameter footings” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"每次澆置後以實際混凝土量與密度更新重量與重心，計算吃水、穩心高度與拖航時的傾斜；浮出與下沉作業前確認潮位、波浪與拖船配置，下沉過程以壓艙水量與四周吃水尺同步監控，確保均勻下沉。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"After each pour update weight and centre of gravity from actual quantities and density and compute draft, metacentric height and heel under tow; before float-out and sinking confirm tide, waves and tug arrangement, and during sinking monitor ballast volumes and draft marks around the perimeter to keep the descent level. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：浮運與下沉計畫要由海事工程師與結構設計者共同簽認，列出每個階段的重量、吃水、穩定性、氣象門檻與中止條件；乾塢閘門與排水系統的檢查要列為浮出前的停留檢查點。","observationEn":"Site practice: Float-out and sinking plans need joint sign-off by the marine engineer and the structural designer, listing weight, draft, stability, weather limits and abort criteria for each stage; inspection of the dock gate and dewatering systems is a hold point before float-out.","failure":"注意干擾：重量或重心估算錯誤，可能使結構在乾塢內擱淺無法浮出，或在拖航中傾斜過大；下沉時壓艙不均造成傾斜就位，會讓基礎在礫石層上偏心受力，並使塔的初始傾斜超出 1/500 的容許值。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Wrong weight or centre-of-gravity estimates can leave the structure grounded in the dock or heeling excessively under tow; uneven ballasting during sinking lands it tilted, loading the gravel eccentrically and pushing the pylon’s initial tilt beyond the 1/500 allowance. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b012-v13-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"每次澆置後以實際混凝土量與密度更新重量與重心，計算吃水、穩心高度與拖航時的傾斜；浮出與下沉作業前確認潮位、波浪與拖船配置，下沉過程以壓艙水量與四周吃水尺同步監控，確保均勻下沉。","textEn":"After each pour update weight and centre of gravity from actual quantities and density and compute draft, metacentric height and heel under tow; before float-out and sinking confirm tide, waves and tug arrangement, and during sinking monitor ballast volumes and draft marks around the perimeter to keep the descent level.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]},{"id":"b012-v13-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"浮運與下沉計畫要由海事工程師與結構設計者共同簽認，列出每個階段的重量、吃水、穩定性、氣象門檻與中止條件；乾塢閘門與排水系統的檢查要列為浮出前的停留檢查點。","textEn":"Float-out and sinking plans need joint sign-off by the marine engineer and the structural designer, listing weight, draft, stability, weather limits and abort criteria for each stage; inspection of the dock gate and dewatering systems is a hold point before float-out.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「90 m 沉箱的乾塢製作與浮運」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Dry-dock casting and floating of the 90 m caissons\"?","options":["每次澆置後以實際混凝土量與密度更新重量與重心，計算吃水、穩心高度與拖航時的傾斜。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","抗震設計的最佳做法永遠是把結構做得更強、更固定。"],"optionsEn":["After each pour update weight and centre of gravity from actual quantities and density and compute draft, metacentric height and heel under tow.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","The best seismic design is always to make the structure stronger and more rigidly fixed."],"answer":0,"explanation":"每次澆置後以實際混凝土量與密度更新重量與重心，計算吃水、穩心高度與拖航時的傾斜；浮出與下沉作業前確認潮位、波浪與拖船配置，下沉過程以壓艙水量與四周吃水尺同步監控，確保均勻下沉。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"After each pour update weight and centre of gravity from actual quantities and density and compute draft, metacentric height and heel under tow; before float-out and sinking confirm tide, waves and tug arrangement, and during sinking monitor ballast volumes and draft marks around the perimeter to keep the descent level. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b012-v13-16","title":"90 m 沉箱的乾塢製作與浮運：失效診斷","titleEn":"Dry-dock casting and floating of the 90 m caissons: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"],"prerequisiteIds":["b012-v13-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「90 m 直徑基礎」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “90 m diameter footings” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"重量或重心估算錯誤，可能使結構在乾塢內擱淺無法浮出，或在拖航中傾斜過大；下沉時壓艙不均造成傾斜就位，會讓基礎在礫石層上偏心受力，並使塔的初始傾斜超出 1/500 的容許值。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Wrong weight or centre-of-gravity estimates can leave the structure grounded in the dock or heeling excessively under tow; uneven ballasting during sinking lands it tilted, loading the gravel eccentrically and pushing the pylon’s initial tilt beyond the 1/500 allowance. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這個方法把大量混凝土作業移到岸邊受控環境，但浮運期間的吃水、穩定性與拖航條件都必須精確計算。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The method moves most concrete work to a controlled shore site, but draft, stability and towing conditions while afloat must be calculated precisely.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「混凝土結構太重，不可能在海上浮運。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Concrete structures are too heavy to float and tow at sea.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b012-v13-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"重量或重心估算錯誤，可能使結構在乾塢內擱淺無法浮出，或在拖航中傾斜過大；下沉時壓艙不均造成傾斜就位，會讓基礎在礫石層上偏心受力，並使塔的初始傾斜超出 1/500 的容許值。","textEn":"Wrong weight or centre-of-gravity estimates can leave the structure grounded in the dock or heeling excessively under tow; uneven ballasting during sinking lands it tilted, loading the gravel eccentrically and pushing the pylon’s initial tilt beyond the 1/500 allowance.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]},{"id":"b012-v13-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「90 m 沉箱的乾塢製作與浮運」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Dry-dock casting and floating of the 90 m caissons\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","重量或重心估算錯誤，可能使結構在乾塢內擱淺無法浮出，或在拖航中傾斜過大。","深海的礫石墊層只是填料，平整度要求可以放寬。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Wrong weight or centre-of-gravity estimates can leave the structure grounded in the dock or heeling excessively under tow.","A deep-water gravel bed is just fill, so its flatness can be relaxed."],"answer":1,"explanation":"重量或重心估算錯誤，可能使結構在乾塢內擱淺無法浮出，或在拖航中傾斜過大；下沉時壓艙不均造成傾斜就位，會讓基礎在礫石層上偏心受力，並使塔的初始傾斜超出 1/500 的容許值。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Wrong weight or centre-of-gravity estimates can leave the structure grounded in the dock or heeling excessively under tow; uneven ballasting during sinking lands it tilted, loading the gravel eccentrically and pushing the pylon’s initial tilt beyond the 1/500 allowance. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b012-v13-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「65 m 水深的海床整備與礫石鋪設公差」與「組合橋面的平衡懸臂架設」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Seabed preparation at 65 m depth and gravel-bed tolerances\" and \"Balanced-cantilever erection of the composite deck\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b012-v13-17","title":"65 m 水深的海床整備與礫石鋪設公差：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Seabed preparation at 65 m depth and gravel-bed tolerances: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"],"prerequisiteIds":["b012-v13-16"],"objective":"說明「張力腿駁船」如何影響里翁—安提里翁大橋的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Tension-leg barge” governs force, deformation or durability in “Rion–Antirion Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"在水深達 65 m 的海峽中，浚挖海床、打入數百根鋼管插入物並鋪設 3 m 礫石層，都必須在穩定的平台上進行。營運單位公開資料指出，承包團隊為此打造專用的張力腿駁船：以錨鏈或錨索拉緊固定在海床上的重物，使駁船在波浪中幾乎不上下起伏，成為深水中的穩定工作平台。礫石層的平整度直接決定沉箱坐落後的傾斜，而塔的傾斜容許只有 1/500，所以水下鋪設的公差比一般海事工程嚴格得多，需要以精密測深與耙平工具反覆修整。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「張力腿駁船」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"In a strait up to 65 m deep, dredging the seabed, driving hundreds of steel inclusions and placing a 3 m gravel layer all need a stable platform. Operator data state that the team built a purpose-made tension-leg barge, held down by taut lines to anchors on the seabed so it barely heaves in waves, giving a stable work platform in deep water. The flatness of the gravel bed determines the tilt of the caisson once landed, and the pylon tilt allowance is only 1/500, so underwater placement tolerances are much tighter than in ordinary marine work and need repeated precise soundings and screeding. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Tension-leg barge” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：基礎直徑 90 m，若礫石面兩端高差 Δ，傾斜 = Δ/90。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: For a 90 m footing, a level difference Δ across the gravel gives a tilt of Δ/90.","failure":"常見誤解：「深海的礫石墊層只是填料，平整度要求可以放寬。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A deep-water gravel bed is just fill, so its flatness can be relaxed.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「張力腿駁船」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Tension-leg barge”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b012-v13-17-k1","title":"65 m 水深的海床整備與礫石鋪設公差","titleEn":"Seabed preparation at 65 m depth and gravel-bed tolerances","text":"在水深達 65 m 的海峽中，浚挖海床、打入數百根鋼管插入物並鋪設 3 m 礫石層，都必須在穩定的平台上進行。營運單位公開資料指出，承包團隊為此打造專用的張力腿駁船：以錨鏈或錨索拉緊固定在海床上的重物，使駁船在波浪中幾乎不上下起伏，成為深水中的穩定工作平台。","textEn":"In a strait up to 65 m deep, dredging the seabed, driving hundreds of steel inclusions and placing a 3 m gravel layer all need a stable platform. Operator data state that the team built a purpose-made tension-leg barge, held down by taut lines to anchors on the seabed so it barely heaves in waves, giving a stable work platform in deep water.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]},{"id":"b012-v13-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：深海的礫石墊層只是填料，平整度要求可以放寬。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A deep-water gravel bed is just fill, so its flatness can be relaxed. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「65 m 水深的海床整備與礫石鋪設公差」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Seabed preparation at 65 m depth and gravel-bed tolerances\" is correct?","options":["深海的礫石墊層只是填料，平整度要求可以放寬。","平衡懸臂只要最後兩側長度相同，中間的施工順序不重要。","在水深達 65 m 的海峽中，浚挖海床、打入數百根鋼管插入物並鋪設 3 m 礫石層，都必須在穩定的平台上進行。"],"optionsEn":["A deep-water gravel bed is just fill, so its flatness can be relaxed.","In balanced cantilever erection only the final equal lengths matter, not the order in between.","In a strait up to 65 m deep, dredging the seabed, driving hundreds of steel inclusions and placing a 3 m gravel layer all need a stable platform."],"answer":2,"explanation":"在水深達 65 m 的海峽中，浚挖海床、打入數百根鋼管插入物並鋪設 3 m 礫石層，都必須在穩定的平台上進行。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"In a strait up to 65 m deep, dredging the seabed, driving hundreds of steel inclusions and placing a 3 m gravel layer all need a stable platform. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b012-v13-18","title":"65 m 水深的海床整備與礫石鋪設公差：定量估算","titleEn":"Seabed preparation at 65 m depth and gravel-bed tolerances: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"],"prerequisiteIds":["b012-v13-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「張力腿駁船」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Tension-leg barge” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：基礎直徑 90 m，若礫石面兩端高差 Δ，傾斜 = Δ/90。容許 1/500 時 Δ = 90/500 = 0.18 m；若只允許用掉一半預算給礫石面，Δ 須小於約 0.09 m。高差 0.10 m 對應傾斜 0.10/90 ≈ 1/900。預算分配為教學假設，1/500 為公開設計值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: For a 90 m footing, a level difference Δ across the gravel gives a tilt of Δ/90. The 1/500 allowance corresponds to Δ = 90/500 = 0.18 m; if only half that budget may be spent on the gravel bed, Δ must stay below about 0.09 m. A 0.10 m difference corresponds to 0.10/90 ≈ 1/900. The budget split is a teaching assumption; 1/500 is the published design value. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：鋪設前後以多音束或高精度單音束測深建立礫石面的數值地形，網格點高差與整體平面度逐項比對公差；必要時以水下攝影或潛水員確認局部異常，沉箱就位後量測塔座傾斜，回算實際礫石面效果。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Before and after placement build a digital terrain of the gravel surface by multibeam or high-precision single-beam sounding, checking grid-point differences and overall flatness against tolerance; confirm local anomalies by underwater video or divers, and after landing measure the pylon base tilt to back-calculate the gravel-bed outcome.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b012-v13-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"基礎直徑 90 m，若礫石面兩端高差 Δ，傾斜 = Δ/90。容許 1/500 時 Δ = 90/500 = 0.18 m；若只允許用掉一半預算給礫石面，Δ 須小於約 0.09 m。高差 0.10 m 對應傾斜 0.10/90 ≈ 1/900。預算分配為教學假設，1/500 為公開設計值。","textEn":"For a 90 m footing, a level difference Δ across the gravel gives a tilt of Δ/90. The 1/500 allowance corresponds to Δ = 90/500 = 0.18 m; if only half that budget may be spent on the gravel bed, Δ must stay below about 0.09 m. A 0.10 m difference corresponds to 0.10/90 ≈ 1/900. The budget split is a teaching assumption; 1/500 is the published design value.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]},{"id":"b012-v13-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「65 m 水深的海床整備與礫石鋪設公差」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Seabed preparation at 65 m depth and gravel-bed tolerances\", which statement holds?","options":["基礎直徑 90 m，若礫石面兩端高差 Δ，傾斜 = Δ/90。","有了即時感測器，就不需要定期做傳統測量。","高強度海工混凝土在 120 年內不需要任何耐久性檢測。"],"optionsEn":["For a 90 m footing, a level difference Δ across the gravel gives a tilt of Δ/90.","With real-time sensors there is no need for periodic conventional surveys.","High-strength marine concrete needs no durability testing over 120 years."],"answer":0,"explanation":"基礎直徑 90 m，若礫石面兩端高差 Δ，傾斜 = Δ/90。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"For a 90 m footing, a level difference Δ across the gravel gives a tilt of Δ/90. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b012-v13-19","title":"65 m 水深的海床整備與礫石鋪設公差：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Seabed preparation at 65 m depth and gravel-bed tolerances: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"],"prerequisiteIds":["b012-v13-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「張力腿駁船」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Tension-leg barge” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"鋪設前後以多音束或高精度單音束測深建立礫石面的數值地形，網格點高差與整體平面度逐項比對公差；必要時以水下攝影或潛水員確認局部異常，沉箱就位後量測塔座傾斜，回算實際礫石面效果。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Before and after placement build a digital terrain of the gravel surface by multibeam or high-precision single-beam sounding, checking grid-point differences and overall flatness against tolerance; confirm local anomalies by underwater video or divers, and after landing measure the pylon base tilt to back-calculate the gravel-bed outcome. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：水下作業的檢查計畫要訂出測深頻率、網格大小、容許高差與重整條件，並把礫石面驗收列為沉箱下沉前的停留檢查點，由業主代表與設計者共同簽認。","observationEn":"Site practice: The underwater inspection plan should set sounding frequency, grid size, allowable differences and rework triggers, with gravel-bed acceptance a hold point before caisson sinking, signed jointly by the owner’s representative and the designer.","failure":"注意干擾：礫石面不平或局部鬆散，沉箱坐落後產生初始傾斜與不均勻接觸，地震時滑移行為也偏離設計；張力腿系統若失效，駁船起伏使插入物定位與打設深度出現誤差。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: An uneven or locally loose gravel surface gives the landed caisson an initial tilt and uneven contact, and makes its seismic sliding behaviour depart from design; if the tension-leg system fails, barge heave introduces errors in inclusion position and driving depth. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b012-v13-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"鋪設前後以多音束或高精度單音束測深建立礫石面的數值地形，網格點高差與整體平面度逐項比對公差；必要時以水下攝影或潛水員確認局部異常，沉箱就位後量測塔座傾斜，回算實際礫石面效果。","textEn":"Before and after placement build a digital terrain of the gravel surface by multibeam or high-precision single-beam sounding, checking grid-point differences and overall flatness against tolerance; confirm local anomalies by underwater video or divers, and after landing measure the pylon base tilt to back-calculate the gravel-bed outcome.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]},{"id":"b012-v13-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"水下作業的檢查計畫要訂出測深頻率、網格大小、容許高差與重整條件，並把礫石面驗收列為沉箱下沉前的停留檢查點，由業主代表與設計者共同簽認。","textEn":"The underwater inspection plan should set sounding frequency, grid size, allowable differences and rework triggers, with gravel-bed acceptance a hold point before caisson sinking, signed jointly by the owner’s representative and the designer.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「65 m 水深的海床整備與礫石鋪設公差」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Seabed preparation at 65 m depth and gravel-bed tolerances\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","鋪設前後以多音束或高精度單音束測深建立礫石面的數值地形，網格點高差與整體平面度逐項比對公差。","橋面懸吊在塔上自由擺動，地震時就不需要任何阻尼裝置。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Before and after placement build a digital terrain of the gravel surface by multibeam or high-precision single-beam sounding, checking grid-point differences and overall flatness against tolerance.","If the deck hangs freely from the pylons, it needs no damping devices in an earthquake."],"answer":1,"explanation":"鋪設前後以多音束或高精度單音束測深建立礫石面的數值地形，網格點高差與整體平面度逐項比對公差；必要時以水下攝影或潛水員確認局部異常，沉箱就位後量測塔座傾斜，回算實際礫石面效果。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Before and after placement build a digital terrain of the gravel surface by multibeam or high-precision single-beam sounding, checking grid-point differences and overall flatness against tolerance; confirm local anomalies by underwater video or divers, and after landing measure the pylon base tilt to back-calculate the gravel-bed outcome. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b012-v13-20","title":"65 m 水深的海床整備與礫石鋪設公差：失效診斷","titleEn":"Seabed preparation at 65 m depth and gravel-bed tolerances: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"],"prerequisiteIds":["b012-v13-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「張力腿駁船」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Tension-leg barge” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"礫石面不平或局部鬆散，沉箱坐落後產生初始傾斜與不均勻接觸，地震時滑移行為也偏離設計；張力腿系統若失效，駁船起伏使插入物定位與打設深度出現誤差。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"An uneven or locally loose gravel surface gives the landed caisson an initial tilt and uneven contact, and makes its seismic sliding behaviour depart from design; if the tension-leg system fails, barge heave introduces errors in inclusion position and driving depth. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：礫石層的平整度直接決定沉箱坐落後的傾斜，而塔的傾斜容許只有 1/500，所以水下鋪設的公差比一般海事工程嚴格得多，需要以精密測深與耙平工具反覆修整。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The flatness of the gravel bed determines the tilt of the caisson once landed, and the pylon tilt allowance is only 1/500, so underwater placement tolerances are much tighter than in ordinary marine work and need repeated precise soundings and screeding.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「深海的礫石墊層只是填料，平整度要求可以放寬。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A deep-water gravel bed is just fill, so its flatness can be relaxed.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b012-v13-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"礫石面不平或局部鬆散，沉箱坐落後產生初始傾斜與不均勻接觸，地震時滑移行為也偏離設計；張力腿系統若失效，駁船起伏使插入物定位與打設深度出現誤差。","textEn":"An uneven or locally loose gravel surface gives the landed caisson an initial tilt and uneven contact, and makes its seismic sliding behaviour depart from design; if the tension-leg system fails, barge heave introduces errors in inclusion position and driving depth.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]},{"id":"b012-v13-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「65 m 水深的海床整備與礫石鋪設公差」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Seabed preparation at 65 m depth and gravel-bed tolerances\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","平衡懸臂只要最後兩側長度相同，中間的施工順序不重要。","礫石面不平或局部鬆散，沉箱坐落後產生初始傾斜與不均勻接觸，地震時滑移行為也偏離設計；張力腿系統若失效，駁船起伏使插入物定位與打設深度出現誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","In balanced cantilever erection only the final equal lengths matter, not the order in between.","An uneven or locally loose gravel surface gives the landed caisson an initial tilt and uneven contact, and makes its seismic sliding behaviour depart from design."],"answer":2,"explanation":"礫石面不平或局部鬆散，沉箱坐落後產生初始傾斜與不均勻接觸，地震時滑移行為也偏離設計；張力腿系統若失效，駁船起伏使插入物定位與打設深度出現誤差。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"An uneven or locally loose gravel surface gives the landed caisson an initial tilt and uneven contact, and makes its seismic sliding behaviour depart from design; if the tension-leg system fails, barge heave introduces errors in inclusion position and driving depth. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b012-v13-21","title":"組合橋面的平衡懸臂架設：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Balanced-cantilever erection of the composite deck: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"],"prerequisiteIds":["b012-v13-20"],"objective":"說明「12 m 預製節段」如何影響里翁—安提里翁大橋的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “12 m precast segments” governs force, deformation or durability in “Rion–Antirion Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"里翁—安提里翁大橋的組合橋面寬 27.2 m，每側兩根 2.2 m 高的鋼板梁，每 4 m 一道橫梁，上覆混凝土橋面板。營運單位公開資料指出，橋面以 12 m 長、約 340 t 的預製節段由浮吊放置，從每座塔向兩側平衡懸臂推進，最快每週約 60 m。平衡懸臂的關鍵在於兩側重量與斜索力保持對稱：只要一側先放節段，塔就要承受一個節段重量乘上懸臂長度的不平衡彎矩，懸臂愈長愈大。因此架設順序、臨時配重與斜索張拉步驟都必須事先排定。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「12 m 預製節段」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The Rion–Antirion composite deck is 27.2 m wide, with two 2.2 m deep steel plate girders on each side, cross girders every 4 m and a concrete deck slab. Operator data state that it was erected in 12 m precast segments of about 340 t placed by floating crane, advancing as balanced cantilevers from each pylon at up to about 60 m a week. The key is keeping weights and stay forces symmetrical on both sides: whenever one side receives a segment first, the pylon carries an unbalanced moment equal to a segment’s weight times the cantilever length, growing as the cantilever lengthens. Erection order, temporary counterweights and stay-stressing steps must therefore be planned in advance. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “12 m precast segments” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：一個 340 t 節段約 340×9.81 ≈ 3,335 kN，若在懸臂長 280 m 處先單側放置，不平衡彎矩 M = 3,335×280 ≈ 933,900 kN·m；每週 60 m 相當於 60/12 = 5 個節段。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: One 340 t segment weighs about 340×9.81 ≈ 3,335 kN; placed on one side at a 280 m cantilever, it creates an unbalanced moment M = 3,335×280 ≈ 933,900 kN·m.","failure":"常見誤解：「平衡懸臂只要最後兩側長度相同，中間的施工順序不重要。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"In balanced cantilever erection only the final equal lengths matter, not the order in between.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「12 m 預製節段」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “12 m precast segments”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b012-v13-21-k1","title":"組合橋面的平衡懸臂架設","titleEn":"Balanced-cantilever erection of the composite deck","text":"里翁—安提里翁大橋的組合橋面寬 27.2 m，每側兩根 2.2 m 高的鋼板梁，每 4 m 一道橫梁，上覆混凝土橋面板。營運單位公開資料指出，橋面以 12 m 長、約 340 t 的預製節段由浮吊放置，從每座塔向兩側平衡懸臂推進，最快每週約 60 m。","textEn":"The Rion–Antirion composite deck is 27.2 m wide, with two 2.2 m deep steel plate girders on each side, cross girders every 4 m and a concrete deck slab. Operator data state that it was erected in 12 m precast segments of about 340 t placed by floating crane, advancing as balanced cantilevers from each pylon at up to about 60 m a week.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]},{"id":"b012-v13-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：平衡懸臂只要最後兩側長度相同，中間的施工順序不重要。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: In balanced cantilever erection only the final equal lengths matter, not the order in between. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「組合橋面的平衡懸臂架設」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Balanced-cantilever erection of the composite deck\" is correct?","options":["里翁—安提里翁大橋的組合橋面寬 27.2 m，每側兩根 2.2 m 高的鋼板梁，每 4 m 一道橫梁，上覆混凝土橋面板。","平衡懸臂只要最後兩側長度相同，中間的施工順序不重要。","感測器越多、取樣越快，監測系統就一定越有用。"],"optionsEn":["The Rion–Antirion composite deck is 27.2 m wide, with two 2.2 m deep steel plate girders on each side, cross girders every 4 m and a concrete deck slab.","In balanced cantilever erection only the final equal lengths matter, not the order in between.","More sensors and faster sampling always make a monitoring system more useful."],"answer":0,"explanation":"里翁—安提里翁大橋的組合橋面寬 27.2 m，每側兩根 2.2 m 高的鋼板梁，每 4 m 一道橫梁，上覆混凝土橋面板。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The Rion–Antirion composite deck is 27.2 m wide, with two 2.2 m deep steel plate girders on each side, cross girders every 4 m and a concrete deck slab. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b012-v13-22","title":"組合橋面的平衡懸臂架設：定量估算","titleEn":"Balanced-cantilever erection of the composite deck: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"],"prerequisiteIds":["b012-v13-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「12 m 預製節段」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “12 m precast segments” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：一個 340 t 節段約 340×9.81 ≈ 3,335 kN，若在懸臂長 280 m 處先單側放置，不平衡彎矩 M = 3,335×280 ≈ 933,900 kN·m；每週 60 m 相當於 60/12 = 5 個節段。若兩側交替並以臨時配重平衡，可把 M 控制在一半以下。懸臂長度為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: One 340 t segment weighs about 340×9.81 ≈ 3,335 kN; placed on one side at a 280 m cantilever, it creates an unbalanced moment M = 3,335×280 ≈ 933,900 kN·m. Sixty metres a week is 60/12 = 5 segments. Alternating sides with temporary counterweights can keep M below half that. The cantilever length is a teaching assumption. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：每個節段就位後量測兩側懸臂端高程、塔頂偏位與新裝斜索的索力，與施工控制模型比較；超出容許時先調整斜索力再進行下一節段；浮吊作業前確認風浪條件與吊重紀錄。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: After each segment is placed, survey both cantilever-tip levels, pylon-top displacement and the new stay’s force and compare with the construction-control model; if outside tolerance, adjust stay forces before the next segment; confirm wind and wave conditions and lift records before each floating-crane operation.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b012-v13-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"一個 340 t 節段約 340×9.81 ≈ 3,335 kN，若在懸臂長 280 m 處先單側放置，不平衡彎矩 M = 3,335×280 ≈ 933,900 kN·m；每週 60 m 相當於 60/12 = 5 個節段。若兩側交替並以臨時配重平衡，可把 M 控制在一半以下。懸臂長度為教學假設。","textEn":"One 340 t segment weighs about 340×9.81 ≈ 3,335 kN; placed on one side at a 280 m cantilever, it creates an unbalanced moment M = 3,335×280 ≈ 933,900 kN·m. Sixty metres a week is 60/12 = 5 segments. Alternating sides with temporary counterweights can keep M below half that. The cantilever length is a teaching assumption.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]},{"id":"b012-v13-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「組合橋面的平衡懸臂架設」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Balanced-cantilever erection of the composite deck\", which statement holds?","options":["斜索是由許多鋼絞線組成的，所以整根斜索不可能突然失效。","一個 340 t 節段約 340×9.81 ≈ 3,335 kN，若在懸臂長 280 m 處先單側放置，不平衡彎矩 M = 3,335×280 ≈ 933,900 kN·m。","抗震設計的最佳做法永遠是把結構做得更強、更固定。"],"optionsEn":["Because a stay is made of many strands, the whole stay can never fail suddenly.","One 340 t segment weighs about 340×9.81 ≈ 3,335 kN; placed on one side at a 280 m cantilever, it creates an unbalanced moment M = 3,335×280 ≈ 933,900 kN·m.","The best seismic design is always to make the structure stronger and more rigidly fixed."],"answer":1,"explanation":"一個 340 t 節段約 340×9.81 ≈ 3,335 kN，若在懸臂長 280 m 處先單側放置，不平衡彎矩 M = 3,335×280 ≈ 933,900 kN·m；每週 60 m 相當於 60/12 = 5 個節段。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"One 340 t segment weighs about 340×9.81 ≈ 3,335 kN; placed on one side at a 280 m cantilever, it creates an unbalanced moment M = 3,335×280 ≈ 933,900 kN·m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b012-v13-23","title":"組合橋面的平衡懸臂架設：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Balanced-cantilever erection of the composite deck: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"],"prerequisiteIds":["b012-v13-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「12 m 預製節段」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “12 m precast segments” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"每個節段就位後量測兩側懸臂端高程、塔頂偏位與新裝斜索的索力，與施工控制模型比較；超出容許時先調整斜索力再進行下一節段；浮吊作業前確認風浪條件與吊重紀錄。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"After each segment is placed, survey both cantilever-tip levels, pylon-top displacement and the new stay’s force and compare with the construction-control model; if outside tolerance, adjust stay forces before the next segment; confirm wind and wave conditions and lift records before each floating-crane operation. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：架設計畫要列出每一步的容許不平衡彎矩、臨時配重位置與量測項目，並規定強風或浮吊故障時的懸臂臨時固定方式；每座塔的合龍視為停留檢查點。","observationEn":"Site practice: The erection plan should list the allowable unbalanced moment, temporary counterweight positions and measurements for every step and define how cantilevers are secured in strong wind or if the floating crane fails; each closure is a hold point.","failure":"注意干擾：不平衡架設超過塔的設計容量，會使塔頂偏位過大、塔身開裂；若相鄰兩個懸臂在合龍時高差過大，需強制頂壓才能對接，會在橋面留下殘餘應力。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Unbalanced erection beyond the pylon’s capacity causes excessive pylon sway and cracking; a large level difference between adjacent cantilevers at closure forces jacking to align them, leaving residual stress in the deck. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b012-v13-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"每個節段就位後量測兩側懸臂端高程、塔頂偏位與新裝斜索的索力，與施工控制模型比較；超出容許時先調整斜索力再進行下一節段；浮吊作業前確認風浪條件與吊重紀錄。","textEn":"After each segment is placed, survey both cantilever-tip levels, pylon-top displacement and the new stay’s force and compare with the construction-control model; if outside tolerance, adjust stay forces before the next segment; confirm wind and wave conditions and lift records before each floating-crane operation.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]},{"id":"b012-v13-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"架設計畫要列出每一步的容許不平衡彎矩、臨時配重位置與量測項目，並規定強風或浮吊故障時的懸臂臨時固定方式；每座塔的合龍視為停留檢查點。","textEn":"The erection plan should list the allowable unbalanced moment, temporary counterweight positions and measurements for every step and define how cantilevers are secured in strong wind or if the floating crane fails; each closure is a hold point.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「組合橋面的平衡懸臂架設」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Balanced-cantilever erection of the composite deck\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","軟弱海床上的大橋基礎一定要用長樁打到岩盤。","每個節段就位後量測兩側懸臂端高程、塔頂偏位與新裝斜索的索力，與施工控制模型比較；超出容許時先調整斜索力再進行下一節段；浮吊作業前確認風浪條件與吊重紀錄。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Bridge foundations on soft seabed must always use long piles driven to rock.","After each segment is placed, survey both cantilever-tip levels, pylon-top displacement and the new stay’s force and compare with the construction-control model."],"answer":2,"explanation":"每個節段就位後量測兩側懸臂端高程、塔頂偏位與新裝斜索的索力，與施工控制模型比較；超出容許時先調整斜索力再進行下一節段；浮吊作業前確認風浪條件與吊重紀錄。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"After each segment is placed, survey both cantilever-tip levels, pylon-top displacement and the new stay’s force and compare with the construction-control model; if outside tolerance, adjust stay forces before the next segment; confirm wind and wave conditions and lift records before each floating-crane operation. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b012-v13-24","title":"組合橋面的平衡懸臂架設：失效診斷","titleEn":"Balanced-cantilever erection of the composite deck: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"],"prerequisiteIds":["b012-v13-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「12 m 預製節段」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “12 m precast segments” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"不平衡架設超過塔的設計容量，會使塔頂偏位過大、塔身開裂；若相鄰兩個懸臂在合龍時高差過大，需強制頂壓才能對接，會在橋面留下殘餘應力。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Unbalanced erection beyond the pylon’s capacity causes excessive pylon sway and cracking; a large level difference between adjacent cantilevers at closure forces jacking to align them, leaving residual stress in the deck. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：因此架設順序、臨時配重與斜索張拉步驟都必須事先排定。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Erection order, temporary counterweights and stay-stressing steps must therefore be planned in advance.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「平衡懸臂只要最後兩側長度相同，中間的施工順序不重要。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"In balanced cantilever erection only the final equal lengths matter, not the order in between.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b012-v13-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"不平衡架設超過塔的設計容量，會使塔頂偏位過大、塔身開裂；若相鄰兩個懸臂在合龍時高差過大，需強制頂壓才能對接，會在橋面留下殘餘應力。","textEn":"Unbalanced erection beyond the pylon’s capacity causes excessive pylon sway and cracking; a large level difference between adjacent cantilevers at closure forces jacking to align them, leaving residual stress in the deck.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]},{"id":"b012-v13-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「組合橋面的平衡懸臂架設」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Balanced-cantilever erection of the composite deck\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["不平衡架設超過塔的設計容量，會使塔頂偏位過大、塔身開裂；若相鄰兩個懸臂在合龍時高差過大，需強制頂壓才能對接，會在橋面留下殘餘應力。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","感測器越多、取樣越快，監測系統就一定越有用。"],"optionsEn":["Unbalanced erection beyond the pylon’s capacity causes excessive pylon sway and cracking.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","More sensors and faster sampling always make a monitoring system more useful."],"answer":0,"explanation":"不平衡架設超過塔的設計容量，會使塔頂偏位過大、塔身開裂；若相鄰兩個懸臂在合龍時高差過大，需強制頂壓才能對接，會在橋面留下殘餘應力。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Unbalanced erection beyond the pylon’s capacity causes excessive pylon sway and cracking; a large level difference between adjacent cantilevers at closure forces jacking to align them, leaving residual stress in the deck. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b012-v13-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「WEASHM 監測系統與事件自動報告」與「測地監測、塔傾斜與構造位移追蹤」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"The WEASHM monitoring system and automatic event reports\" and \"Geodetic monitoring, pylon tilt and tectonic tracking\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b012-v13-25","title":"WEASHM 監測系統與事件自動報告：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"The WEASHM monitoring system and automatic event reports: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"],"prerequisiteIds":["b012-v13-24"],"objective":"說明「限制器荷重計」如何影響里翁—安提里翁大橋的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Restrainer load cells” governs force, deformation or durability in “Rion–Antirion Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"營運單位公開資料指出，大橋的監測系統（WEASHM）有超過 100 個感測器、約 300 個通道，分布於塔、橋面、斜索與伸縮縫，以 100 Hz 取樣，量測荷重、斜索振動、橋面與塔振動、伸縮縫位移，以及風速風向與氣溫、橋面溫度。資料在四座塔內先以硬體處理並與門檻比較，再經光纖送到營運大樓與控制室；地震或強風等特殊事件開始 5 分鐘後會自動寄出報告。限制器上的荷重計特別重要，因為它直接告訴營運者熔斷元件是否接近或已經斷開，以及地震後是否需要重新校準。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「限制器荷重計」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Operator data state that the bridge’s monitoring system (WEASHM) has more than 100 sensors and about 300 channels on pylons, deck, stays and expansion joints, sampling at 100 Hz to measure loads, stay vibration, deck and pylon vibration and joint displacement, as well as wind speed and direction, air and deck temperature. Data are processed in hardware inside the four pylons and compared with thresholds, then sent by optical fibre to the operations building and control room; an automatic report is emailed 5 minutes after a special event such as an earthquake or high wind begins. The load cells on the restrainers are especially important, telling the operator whether the fuses are near breaking or have broken and whether recalibration is needed after an earthquake. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Restrainer load cells” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：資料量 = 通道數 × 取樣率 × 位元組 × 秒數 = 300×100×4×86,400 ≈ 1.04×10¹⁰ bytes，約 10.4 GB/日；100 Hz 取樣的可用頻寬上限（奈奎斯特頻率）為 50 Hz，足以涵蓋斜索與橋面的主要模態。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Data volume = channels × sampling rate × bytes × seconds = 300×100×4×86,400 ≈ 1.04×10¹⁰ bytes, about 10.4 GB per day; 100 Hz sampling gives a usable bandwidth up to the 50 Hz Nyquist frequency, enough for the main stay and deck modes.","failure":"常見誤解：「感測器越多、取樣越快，監測系統就一定越有用。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"More sensors and faster sampling always make a monitoring system more useful.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「限制器荷重計」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Restrainer load cells”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b012-v13-25-k1","title":"WEASHM 監測系統與事件自動報告","titleEn":"The WEASHM monitoring system and automatic event reports","text":"營運單位公開資料指出，大橋的監測系統（WEASHM）有超過 100 個感測器、約 300 個通道，分布於塔、橋面、斜索與伸縮縫，以 100 Hz 取樣，量測荷重、斜索振動、橋面與塔振動、伸縮縫位移，以及風速風向與氣溫、橋面溫度。資料在四座塔內先以硬體處理並與門檻比較，再經光纖送到營運大樓與控制室；地震或強風等特殊事件開始 5 分鐘後會自動寄出報告。","textEn":"Operator data state that the bridge’s monitoring system (WEASHM) has more than 100 sensors and about 300 channels on pylons, deck, stays and expansion joints, sampling at 100 Hz to measure loads, stay vibration, deck and pylon vibration and joint displacement, as well as wind speed and direction, air and deck temperature. Data are processed in hardware inside the four pylons and compared with thresholds, then sent by optical fibre to the operations building and control room; an automatic report is emailed 5 minutes after a special event such as an earthquake or high wind begins.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]},{"id":"b012-v13-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：感測器越多、取樣越快，監測系統就一定越有用。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: More sensors and faster sampling always make a monitoring system more useful. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「WEASHM 監測系統與事件自動報告」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"The WEASHM monitoring system and automatic event reports\" is correct?","options":["感測器越多、取樣越快，監測系統就一定越有用。","營運單位公開資料指出，大橋的監測系統（WEASHM）有超過 100 個感測器、約 300 個通道，分布於塔、橋面、斜索與伸縮縫，以 100 Hz 取樣，量測荷重、斜索振動、橋面與塔振動、伸縮縫位移，以及風速風向與氣溫、橋面溫度。","有了即時感測器，就不需要定期做傳統測量。"],"optionsEn":["More sensors and faster sampling always make a monitoring system more useful.","Operator data state that the bridge’s monitoring system (WEASHM) has more than 100 sensors and about 300 channels on pylons, deck, stays and expansion joints, sampling at 100 Hz to measure loads, stay vibration, deck and pylon vibration and joint displacement, as well as wind speed and direction, air and deck temperature.","With real-time sensors there is no need for periodic conventional surveys."],"answer":1,"explanation":"營運單位公開資料指出，大橋的監測系統（WEASHM）有超過 100 個感測器、約 300 個通道，分布於塔、橋面、斜索與伸縮縫，以 100 Hz 取樣，量測荷重、斜索振動、橋面與塔振動、伸縮縫位移，以及風速風向與氣溫、橋面溫度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Operator data state that the bridge’s monitoring system (WEASHM) has more than 100 sensors and about 300 channels on pylons, deck, stays and expansion joints, sampling at 100 Hz to measure loads, stay vibration, deck and pylon vibration and joint displacement, as well as wind speed and direction, air and deck temperature. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b012-v13-26","title":"WEASHM 監測系統與事件自動報告：定量估算","titleEn":"The WEASHM monitoring system and automatic event reports: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"],"prerequisiteIds":["b012-v13-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「限制器荷重計」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Restrainer load cells” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：資料量 = 通道數 × 取樣率 × 位元組 × 秒數 = 300×100×4×86,400 ≈ 1.04×10¹⁰ bytes，約 10.4 GB/日；100 Hz 取樣的可用頻寬上限（奈奎斯特頻率）為 50 Hz，足以涵蓋斜索與橋面的主要模態。每點 4 bytes 為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Data volume = channels × sampling rate × bytes × seconds = 300×100×4×86,400 ≈ 1.04×10¹⁰ bytes, about 10.4 GB per day; 100 Hz sampling gives a usable bandwidth up to the 50 Hz Nyquist frequency, enough for the main stay and deck modes. Four bytes per sample is a teaching assumption. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：定期以人工量測（例如振動法索力、手持加速度計）比對感測器讀值，檢查漂移與時間同步；以已知事件（強風日、重車通過）驗證門檻與自動報告流程是否正確觸發，並保存原始資料與處理參數。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Periodically compare sensor readings with manual measurements such as vibration-based stay force or handheld accelerometers, checking drift and time synchronisation; use known events such as high-wind days or heavy vehicles to confirm thresholds and automatic reporting trigger correctly, and archive raw data with processing parameters.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b012-v13-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"資料量 = 通道數 × 取樣率 × 位元組 × 秒數 = 300×100×4×86,400 ≈ 1.04×10¹⁰ bytes，約 10.4 GB/日；100 Hz 取樣的可用頻寬上限（奈奎斯特頻率）為 50 Hz，足以涵蓋斜索與橋面的主要模態。每點 4 bytes 為教學假設。","textEn":"Data volume = channels × sampling rate × bytes × seconds = 300×100×4×86,400 ≈ 1.04×10¹⁰ bytes, about 10.4 GB per day; 100 Hz sampling gives a usable bandwidth up to the 50 Hz Nyquist frequency, enough for the main stay and deck modes. Four bytes per sample is a teaching assumption.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]},{"id":"b012-v13-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「WEASHM 監測系統與事件自動報告」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"The WEASHM monitoring system and automatic event reports\", which statement holds?","options":["高強度海工混凝土在 120 年內不需要任何耐久性檢測。","橋面懸吊在塔上自由擺動，地震時就不需要任何阻尼裝置。","資料量 = 通道數 × 取樣率 × 位元組 × 秒數 = 300×100×4×86,400 ≈ 1.04×10¹⁰ bytes，約 10.4 GB/日。"],"optionsEn":["High-strength marine concrete needs no durability testing over 120 years.","If the deck hangs freely from the pylons, it needs no damping devices in an earthquake.","Data volume = channels × sampling rate × bytes × seconds = 300×100×4×86,400 ≈ 1.04×10¹⁰ bytes, about 10.4 GB per day."],"answer":2,"explanation":"資料量 = 通道數 × 取樣率 × 位元組 × 秒數 = 300×100×4×86,400 ≈ 1.04×10¹⁰ bytes，約 10.4 GB/日；100 Hz 取樣的可用頻寬上限（奈奎斯特頻率）為 50 Hz，足以涵蓋斜索與橋面的主要模態。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Data volume = channels × sampling rate × bytes × seconds = 300×100×4×86,400 ≈ 1.04×10¹⁰ bytes, about 10.4 GB per day; 100 Hz sampling gives a usable bandwidth up to the 50 Hz Nyquist frequency, enough for the main stay and deck modes. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b012-v13-27","title":"WEASHM 監測系統與事件自動報告：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"The WEASHM monitoring system and automatic event reports: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"],"prerequisiteIds":["b012-v13-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「限制器荷重計」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Restrainer load cells” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"定期以人工量測（例如振動法索力、手持加速度計）比對感測器讀值，檢查漂移與時間同步；以已知事件（強風日、重車通過）驗證門檻與自動報告流程是否正確觸發，並保存原始資料與處理參數。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Periodically compare sensor readings with manual measurements such as vibration-based stay force or handheld accelerometers, checking drift and time synchronisation; use known events such as high-wind days or heavy vehicles to confirm thresholds and automatic reporting trigger correctly, and archive raw data with processing parameters. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：監測系統交接要包含感測器清單、校正紀錄、門檻邏輯、自動報告格式與事件後的檢查流程，並明訂誰在收到報告後多少時間內決定封橋或放行。","observationEn":"Site practice: Monitoring handover should include the sensor list, calibration records, threshold logic, report format and post-event inspection procedure, and state who decides closure or reopening and within what time after a report arrives.","failure":"注意干擾：門檻設定只依設計值而未考慮正常季節變化，會產生大量誤報，使營運人員忽略警報；感測器失效或時間不同步若未被發現，地震後的報告可能遺漏關鍵資訊，延誤檢查與交通管制決策。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Thresholds set from design values without normal seasonal variation generate floods of false alarms that operators learn to ignore; undetected sensor failure or loss of synchronisation can leave key information out of a post-earthquake report, delaying inspection and traffic decisions. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b012-v13-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"定期以人工量測（例如振動法索力、手持加速度計）比對感測器讀值，檢查漂移與時間同步；以已知事件（強風日、重車通過）驗證門檻與自動報告流程是否正確觸發，並保存原始資料與處理參數。","textEn":"Periodically compare sensor readings with manual measurements such as vibration-based stay force or handheld accelerometers, checking drift and time synchronisation; use known events such as high-wind days or heavy vehicles to confirm thresholds and automatic reporting trigger correctly, and archive raw data with processing parameters.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]},{"id":"b012-v13-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"監測系統交接要包含感測器清單、校正紀錄、門檻邏輯、自動報告格式與事件後的檢查流程，並明訂誰在收到報告後多少時間內決定封橋或放行。","textEn":"Monitoring handover should include the sensor list, calibration records, threshold logic, report format and post-event inspection procedure, and state who decides closure or reopening and within what time after a report arrives.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「WEASHM 監測系統與事件自動報告」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"The WEASHM monitoring system and automatic event reports\"?","options":["定期以人工量測（例如振動法索力、手持加速度計）比對感測器讀值，檢查漂移與時間同步。","量測時不必記錄溫度、日照、風與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","混凝土結構太重，不可能在海上浮運。"],"optionsEn":["Periodically compare sensor readings with manual measurements such as vibration-based stay force or handheld accelerometers, checking drift and time synchronisation.","Temperature, sunshine, wind and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Concrete structures are too heavy to float and tow at sea."],"answer":0,"explanation":"定期以人工量測（例如振動法索力、手持加速度計）比對感測器讀值，檢查漂移與時間同步；以已知事件（強風日、重車通過）驗證門檻與自動報告流程是否正確觸發，並保存原始資料與處理參數。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Periodically compare sensor readings with manual measurements such as vibration-based stay force or handheld accelerometers, checking drift and time synchronisation; use known events such as high-wind days or heavy vehicles to confirm thresholds and automatic reporting trigger correctly, and archive raw data with processing parameters. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b012-v13-28","title":"WEASHM 監測系統與事件自動報告：失效診斷","titleEn":"The WEASHM monitoring system and automatic event reports: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"],"prerequisiteIds":["b012-v13-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「限制器荷重計」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Restrainer load cells” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"門檻設定只依設計值而未考慮正常季節變化，會產生大量誤報，使營運人員忽略警報；感測器失效或時間不同步若未被發現，地震後的報告可能遺漏關鍵資訊，延誤檢查與交通管制決策。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Thresholds set from design values without normal seasonal variation generate floods of false alarms that operators learn to ignore; undetected sensor failure or loss of synchronisation can leave key information out of a post-earthquake report, delaying inspection and traffic decisions. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：限制器上的荷重計特別重要，因為它直接告訴營運者熔斷元件是否接近或已經斷開，以及地震後是否需要重新校準。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The load cells on the restrainers are especially important, telling the operator whether the fuses are near breaking or have broken and whether recalibration is needed after an earthquake.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「感測器越多、取樣越快，監測系統就一定越有用。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"More sensors and faster sampling always make a monitoring system more useful.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b012-v13-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"門檻設定只依設計值而未考慮正常季節變化，會產生大量誤報，使營運人員忽略警報；感測器失效或時間不同步若未被發現，地震後的報告可能遺漏關鍵資訊，延誤檢查與交通管制決策。","textEn":"Thresholds set from design values without normal seasonal variation generate floods of false alarms that operators learn to ignore; undetected sensor failure or loss of synchronisation can leave key information out of a post-earthquake report, delaying inspection and traffic decisions.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]},{"id":"b012-v13-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「WEASHM 監測系統與事件自動報告」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"The WEASHM monitoring system and automatic event reports\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","門檻設定只依設計值而未考慮正常季節變化，會產生大量誤報，使營運人員忽略警報。","有了即時感測器，就不需要定期做傳統測量。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Thresholds set from design values without normal seasonal variation generate floods of false alarms that operators learn to ignore.","With real-time sensors there is no need for periodic conventional surveys."],"answer":1,"explanation":"門檻設定只依設計值而未考慮正常季節變化，會產生大量誤報，使營運人員忽略警報；感測器失效或時間不同步若未被發現，地震後的報告可能遺漏關鍵資訊，延誤檢查與交通管制決策。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Thresholds set from design values without normal seasonal variation generate floods of false alarms that operators learn to ignore; undetected sensor failure or loss of synchronisation can leave key information out of a post-earthquake report, delaying inspection and traffic decisions. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b012-v13-29","title":"測地監測、塔傾斜與構造位移追蹤：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Geodetic monitoring, pylon tilt and tectonic tracking: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"],"prerequisiteIds":["b012-v13-28"],"objective":"說明「岸邊與墩位測地點」如何影響里翁—安提里翁大橋的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Shore and pier geodetic points” governs force, deformation or durability in “Rion–Antirion Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"感測器擅長記錄動態反應，但緩慢的構造位移、基礎沉陷與塔的傾斜需要另一種工具。營運單位公開資料指出，大橋定期以傳統測地方法（非永久系統）量測橋梁幾何以及兩岸與各墩位的構造位移。這些量測把每座塔、每個基礎放進同一個座標系統，追蹤多年下來的相對位移、沉陷與傾斜是否仍在設計預算內。塔高很大，即使很小的傾斜也會在塔頂放大成明顯位移，進而改變斜索幾何與索力，因此傾斜量測同時是結構與斜索系統的健康指標。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「岸邊與墩位測地點」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Sensors excel at dynamic response, but slow tectonic movement, foundation settlement and pylon tilt need another tool. Operator data state that bridge geometry and tectonic movements at the shores and pier locations are measured at regular intervals by classical geodetic survey rather than a permanent system. These surveys place every pylon and footing in one coordinate system and track whether relative displacement, settlement and tilt over the years remain within the design budget. Because the pylons are tall, even a small tilt is magnified into a visible top displacement that changes stay geometry and forces, so tilt is a health indicator for both the structure and its stay system. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Shore and pier geodetic points” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：塔頂偏位 = 傾斜 × 高度。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Pylon-top offset = tilt × height.","failure":"常見誤解：「有了即時感測器，就不需要定期做傳統測量。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"With real-time sensors there is no need for periodic conventional surveys.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「岸邊與墩位測地點」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Shore and pier geodetic points”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b012-v13-29-k1","title":"測地監測、塔傾斜與構造位移追蹤","titleEn":"Geodetic monitoring, pylon tilt and tectonic tracking","text":"感測器擅長記錄動態反應，但緩慢的構造位移、基礎沉陷與塔的傾斜需要另一種工具。營運單位公開資料指出，大橋定期以傳統測地方法（非永久系統）量測橋梁幾何以及兩岸與各墩位的構造位移。","textEn":"Sensors excel at dynamic response, but slow tectonic movement, foundation settlement and pylon tilt need another tool. Operator data state that bridge geometry and tectonic movements at the shores and pier locations are measured at regular intervals by classical geodetic survey rather than a permanent system.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]},{"id":"b012-v13-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：有了即時感測器，就不需要定期做傳統測量。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: With real-time sensors there is no need for periodic conventional surveys. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「測地監測、塔傾斜與構造位移追蹤」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Geodetic monitoring, pylon tilt and tectonic tracking\" is correct?","options":["有了即時感測器，就不需要定期做傳統測量。","斜索是由許多鋼絞線組成的，所以整根斜索不可能突然失效。","感測器擅長記錄動態反應，但緩慢的構造位移、基礎沉陷與塔的傾斜需要另一種工具。"],"optionsEn":["With real-time sensors there is no need for periodic conventional surveys.","Because a stay is made of many strands, the whole stay can never fail suddenly.","Sensors excel at dynamic response, but slow tectonic movement, foundation settlement and pylon tilt need another tool."],"answer":2,"explanation":"感測器擅長記錄動態反應，但緩慢的構造位移、基礎沉陷與塔的傾斜需要另一種工具。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Sensors excel at dynamic response, but slow tectonic movement, foundation settlement and pylon tilt need another tool. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b012-v13-30","title":"測地監測、塔傾斜與構造位移追蹤：定量估算","titleEn":"Geodetic monitoring, pylon tilt and tectonic tracking: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"],"prerequisiteIds":["b012-v13-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「岸邊與墩位測地點」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Shore and pier geodetic points” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：塔頂偏位 = 傾斜 × 高度。若塔座以上高度取 160 m，容許傾斜 1/500 對應 160/500 = 0.32 m；若量測到傾斜 1/2,000，塔頂偏位只有約 0.08 m，仍在預算的四分之一。高度為教學假設，1/500 為公開設計值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Pylon-top offset = tilt × height. Taking 160 m above the pylon base, the 1/500 allowance corresponds to 160/500 = 0.32 m; a measured tilt of 1/2,000 gives only about 0.08 m, a quarter of the budget. The height is a teaching assumption; 1/500 is the published design value. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以岸上穩定基準點建立控制網，定期以 GNSS 與精密水準量測各墩基礎與塔頂標誌，所有量測修正到同一溫度與時刻；結果與前次及設計預測比較，若相對位移或傾斜速率改變，加密量測頻率並檢討伸縮縫與阻尼器剩餘行程。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Establish a control network from stable shore benchmarks and survey pier footings and pylon-top targets periodically by GNSS and precise levelling, correcting all readings to a common temperature and time; compare with previous surveys and design predictions, and if relative displacement or tilt rates change, survey more often and review remaining joint and damper travel.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b012-v13-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"塔頂偏位 = 傾斜 × 高度。若塔座以上高度取 160 m，容許傾斜 1/500 對應 160/500 = 0.32 m；若量測到傾斜 1/2,000，塔頂偏位只有約 0.08 m，仍在預算的四分之一。高度為教學假設，1/500 為公開設計值。","textEn":"Pylon-top offset = tilt × height. Taking 160 m above the pylon base, the 1/500 allowance corresponds to 160/500 = 0.32 m; a measured tilt of 1/2,000 gives only about 0.08 m, a quarter of the budget. The height is a teaching assumption; 1/500 is the published design value.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]},{"id":"b012-v13-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「測地監測、塔傾斜與構造位移追蹤」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Geodetic monitoring, pylon tilt and tectonic tracking\", which statement holds?","options":["塔頂偏位 = 傾斜 × 高度。","抗震設計的最佳做法永遠是把結構做得更強、更固定。","軟弱海床上的大橋基礎一定要用長樁打到岩盤。"],"optionsEn":["Pylon-top offset = tilt × height.","The best seismic design is always to make the structure stronger and more rigidly fixed.","Bridge foundations on soft seabed must always use long piles driven to rock."],"answer":0,"explanation":"塔頂偏位 = 傾斜 × 高度。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Pylon-top offset = tilt × height. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b012-v13-31","title":"測地監測、塔傾斜與構造位移追蹤：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Geodetic monitoring, pylon tilt and tectonic tracking: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"],"prerequisiteIds":["b012-v13-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「岸邊與墩位測地點」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Shore and pier geodetic points” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以岸上穩定基準點建立控制網，定期以 GNSS 與精密水準量測各墩基礎與塔頂標誌，所有量測修正到同一溫度與時刻；結果與前次及設計預測比較，若相對位移或傾斜速率改變，加密量測頻率並檢討伸縮縫與阻尼器剩餘行程。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Establish a control network from stable shore benchmarks and survey pier footings and pylon-top targets periodically by GNSS and precise levelling, correcting all readings to a common temperature and time; compare with previous surveys and design predictions, and if relative displacement or tilt rates change, survey more often and review remaining joint and damper travel. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：測量計畫應規定基準點的保護與複核、量測時段（清晨溫度均勻時）、精度要求與成果格式；地震後必做一次全橋測地量測並與上次結果比較，作為開放交通決策的依據之一。","observationEn":"Site practice: The survey plan should protect and recheck benchmarks, fix measurement times at dawn when temperature is uniform, and define accuracy and reporting format; after any earthquake a full geodetic survey compared with the previous one is mandatory input to the reopening decision.","failure":"注意干擾：若量測沒有修正日照溫度，塔頂的熱偏位會被誤判為基礎傾斜；若量測間隔太長，地震後的永久位移可能未被及時發現，伸縮縫與阻尼器在下一次事件中已無足夠行程。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Without solar temperature correction, thermal sway at the pylon top can be mistaken for footing tilt; with too long an interval, permanent displacement after an earthquake may go unnoticed and joints and dampers may lack travel for the next event. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b012-v13-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以岸上穩定基準點建立控制網，定期以 GNSS 與精密水準量測各墩基礎與塔頂標誌，所有量測修正到同一溫度與時刻；結果與前次及設計預測比較，若相對位移或傾斜速率改變，加密量測頻率並檢討伸縮縫與阻尼器剩餘行程。","textEn":"Establish a control network from stable shore benchmarks and survey pier footings and pylon-top targets periodically by GNSS and precise levelling, correcting all readings to a common temperature and time; compare with previous surveys and design predictions, and if relative displacement or tilt rates change, survey more often and review remaining joint and damper travel.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]},{"id":"b012-v13-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"測量計畫應規定基準點的保護與複核、量測時段（清晨溫度均勻時）、精度要求與成果格式；地震後必做一次全橋測地量測並與上次結果比較，作為開放交通決策的依據之一。","textEn":"The survey plan should protect and recheck benchmarks, fix measurement times at dawn when temperature is uniform, and define accuracy and reporting format; after any earthquake a full geodetic survey compared with the previous one is mandatory input to the reopening decision.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「測地監測、塔傾斜與構造位移追蹤」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Geodetic monitoring, pylon tilt and tectonic tracking\"?","options":["沿用另一座橋或另一棟建築的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","以岸上穩定基準點建立控制網，定期以 GNSS 與精密水準量測各墩基礎與塔頂標誌，所有量測修正到同一溫度與時刻。","深海的礫石墊層只是填料，平整度要求可以放寬。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another bridge or building counts as verifying this structure.","Establish a control network from stable shore benchmarks and survey pier footings and pylon-top targets periodically by GNSS and precise levelling, correcting all readings to a common temperature and time.","A deep-water gravel bed is just fill, so its flatness can be relaxed."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以岸上穩定基準點建立控制網，定期以 GNSS 與精密水準量測各墩基礎與塔頂標誌，所有量測修正到同一溫度與時刻；結果與前次及設計預測比較，若相對位移或傾斜速率改變，加密量測頻率並檢討伸縮縫與阻尼器剩餘行程。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Establish a control network from stable shore benchmarks and survey pier footings and pylon-top targets periodically by GNSS and precise levelling, correcting all readings to a common temperature and time; compare with previous surveys and design predictions, and if relative displacement or tilt rates change, survey more often and review remaining joint and damper travel. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b012-v13-32","title":"測地監測、塔傾斜與構造位移追蹤：失效診斷","titleEn":"Geodetic monitoring, pylon tilt and tectonic tracking: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"],"prerequisiteIds":["b012-v13-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「岸邊與墩位測地點」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Shore and pier geodetic points” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若量測沒有修正日照溫度，塔頂的熱偏位會被誤判為基礎傾斜；若量測間隔太長，地震後的永久位移可能未被及時發現，伸縮縫與阻尼器在下一次事件中已無足夠行程。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Without solar temperature correction, thermal sway at the pylon top can be mistaken for footing tilt; with too long an interval, permanent displacement after an earthquake may go unnoticed and joints and dampers may lack travel for the next event. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：塔高很大，即使很小的傾斜也會在塔頂放大成明顯位移，進而改變斜索幾何與索力，因此傾斜量測同時是結構與斜索系統的健康指標。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Because the pylons are tall, even a small tilt is magnified into a visible top displacement that changes stay geometry and forces, so tilt is a health indicator for both the structure and its stay system.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「有了即時感測器，就不需要定期做傳統測量。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"With real-time sensors there is no need for periodic conventional surveys.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b012-v13-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若量測沒有修正日照溫度，塔頂的熱偏位會被誤判為基礎傾斜；若量測間隔太長，地震後的永久位移可能未被及時發現，伸縮縫與阻尼器在下一次事件中已無足夠行程。","textEn":"Without solar temperature correction, thermal sway at the pylon top can be mistaken for footing tilt; with too long an interval, permanent displacement after an earthquake may go unnoticed and joints and dampers may lack travel for the next event.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]},{"id":"b012-v13-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「測地監測、塔傾斜與構造位移追蹤」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Geodetic monitoring, pylon tilt and tectonic tracking\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","斜索是由許多鋼絞線組成的，所以整根斜索不可能突然失效。","若量測沒有修正日照溫度，塔頂的熱偏位會被誤判為基礎傾斜；若量測間隔太長，地震後的永久位移可能未被及時發現，伸縮縫與阻尼器在下一次事件中已無足夠行程。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Because a stay is made of many strands, the whole stay can never fail suddenly.","Without solar temperature correction, thermal sway at the pylon top can be mistaken for footing tilt."],"answer":2,"explanation":"若量測沒有修正日照溫度，塔頂的熱偏位會被誤判為基礎傾斜；若量測間隔太長，地震後的永久位移可能未被及時發現，伸縮縫與阻尼器在下一次事件中已無足夠行程。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Without solar temperature correction, thermal sway at the pylon top can be mistaken for footing tilt; with too long an interval, permanent displacement after an earthquake may go unnoticed and joints and dampers may lack travel for the next event. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b012-v13-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「雷擊、斜索火災與單索更換」與「海洋混凝土耐久與 120 年檢查維護」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Lightning, stay fire and single-stay replacement\" and \"Marine concrete durability and 120-year inspection\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b012-v13-33","title":"雷擊、斜索火災與單索更換：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Lightning, stay fire and single-stay replacement: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"],"prerequisiteIds":["b012-v13-32"],"objective":"說明「M1 塔斜索」如何影響里翁—安提里翁大橋的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Stays at pylon M1” governs force, deformation or durability in “Rion–Antirion Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"2005 年 1 月 28 日，通車約半年後，大橋 M1 塔頂附近一根斜索因雷擊引起火災而斷落橋面，交通隨即中斷，修復後重新開放。斜索系統供應商公開資料指出，其後在更換受損斜索的同時，為斜索加裝了雷擊防護。斜索斷失是斜張橋必須設計的意外工況：斷索瞬間釋放的能量使相鄰斜索與橋面產生動力放大，力量重新分配到鄰索；設計必須確認鄰索與橋面在這個工況下不會連鎖破壞，同時要有可以在交通管制下更換單索的程序。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「M1 塔斜索」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"On 28 January 2005, about six months after opening, a stay near the top of pylon M1 failed after a lightning strike started a fire, and fell onto the deck; traffic was stopped and the bridge reopened after repair. The stay supplier’s public material states that lightning protection was installed while the damaged stay was replaced. Stay loss is an accidental case every cable-stayed bridge must be designed for: the sudden release of energy dynamically amplifies the response of neighbouring stays and the deck as force redistributes; design must confirm that neighbours and deck do not fail progressively and that a single stay can be replaced under traffic management. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Stays at pylon M1” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：61 股鋼絞線斜索破斷力 = 61×150 mm²×1,770 MPa ≈ 16,200 kN。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: A 61-strand stay has a breaking force of 61×150 mm²×1,770 MPa ≈ 16,200 kN.","failure":"常見誤解：「斜索是由許多鋼絞線組成的，所以整根斜索不可能突然失效。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Because a stay is made of many strands, the whole stay can never fail suddenly.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「M1 塔斜索」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Stays at pylon M1”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b012-v13-33-k1","title":"雷擊、斜索火災與單索更換","titleEn":"Lightning, stay fire and single-stay replacement","text":"2005 年 1 月 28 日，通車約半年後，大橋 M1 塔頂附近一根斜索因雷擊引起火災而斷落橋面，交通隨即中斷，修復後重新開放。斜索系統供應商公開資料指出，其後在更換受損斜索的同時，為斜索加裝了雷擊防護。","textEn":"On 28 January 2005, about six months after opening, a stay near the top of pylon M1 failed after a lightning strike started a fire, and fell onto the deck; traffic was stopped and the bridge reopened after repair. The stay supplier’s public material states that lightning protection was installed while the damaged stay was replaced.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]},{"id":"b012-v13-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：斜索是由許多鋼絞線組成的，所以整根斜索不可能突然失效。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Because a stay is made of many strands, the whole stay can never fail suddenly. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「雷擊、斜索火災與單索更換」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Lightning, stay fire and single-stay replacement\" is correct?","options":["2005 年 1 月 28 日，通車約半年後，大橋 M1 塔頂附近一根斜索因雷擊引起火災而斷落橋面，交通隨即中斷，修復後重新開放。","斜索是由許多鋼絞線組成的，所以整根斜索不可能突然失效。","高強度海工混凝土在 120 年內不需要任何耐久性檢測。"],"optionsEn":["On 28 January 2005, about six months after opening, a stay near the top of pylon M1 failed after a lightning strike started a fire, and fell onto the deck.","Because a stay is made of many strands, the whole stay can never fail suddenly.","High-strength marine concrete needs no durability testing over 120 years."],"answer":0,"explanation":"2005 年 1 月 28 日，通車約半年後，大橋 M1 塔頂附近一根斜索因雷擊引起火災而斷落橋面，交通隨即中斷，修復後重新開放。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"On 28 January 2005, about six months after opening, a stay near the top of pylon M1 failed after a lightning strike started a fire, and fell onto the deck; traffic was stopped and the bridge reopened after repair. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b012-v13-34","title":"雷擊、斜索火災與單索更換：定量估算","titleEn":"Lightning, stay fire and single-stay replacement: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"],"prerequisiteIds":["b012-v13-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「M1 塔斜索」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Stays at pylon M1” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：61 股鋼絞線斜索破斷力 = 61×150 mm²×1,770 MPa ≈ 16,200 kN。若失去一根 5,000 kN 的斜索，取動力放大係數 2.0、相鄰索分擔 35%，鄰索增量 = 0.35×2.0×5,000 = 3,500 kN，總力 8,500 kN，約為破斷力的 52%。股數、索力與分擔比為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: A 61-strand stay has a breaking force of 61×150 mm²×1,770 MPa ≈ 16,200 kN. If a 5,000 kN neighbour is lost, with a dynamic amplification factor of 2.0 and 35% picked up by the adjacent stay, the increment is 0.35×2.0×5,000 = 3,500 kN for a total of 8,500 kN, about 52% of breaking force. Strand count, force and share are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以非線性動力分析模擬各代表性斜索的突然斷失，檢查鄰索應力比、橋面彎矩與塔的反應；雷擊防護系統依相關防雷標準驗證接地與導通，更換斜索時以荷重計與測量監控臨時索力與橋面線形。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Simulate sudden loss of representative stays with nonlinear dynamic analysis, checking neighbour stress ratios, deck moments and pylon response; verify lightning protection grounding and continuity under the relevant lightning standard, and monitor temporary forces and deck profile with load cells and survey during stay replacement.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b012-v13-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"61 股鋼絞線斜索破斷力 = 61×150 mm²×1,770 MPa ≈ 16,200 kN。若失去一根 5,000 kN 的斜索，取動力放大係數 2.0、相鄰索分擔 35%，鄰索增量 = 0.35×2.0×5,000 = 3,500 kN，總力 8,500 kN，約為破斷力的 52%。股數、索力與分擔比為教學假設。","textEn":"A 61-strand stay has a breaking force of 61×150 mm²×1,770 MPa ≈ 16,200 kN. If a 5,000 kN neighbour is lost, with a dynamic amplification factor of 2.0 and 35% picked up by the adjacent stay, the increment is 0.35×2.0×5,000 = 3,500 kN for a total of 8,500 kN, about 52% of breaking force. Strand count, force and share are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]},{"id":"b012-v13-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「雷擊、斜索火災與單索更換」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Lightning, stay fire and single-stay replacement\", which statement holds?","options":["橋面懸吊在塔上自由擺動，地震時就不需要任何阻尼裝置。","61 股鋼絞線斜索破斷力 = 61×150 mm²×1,770 MPa ≈ 16,200 kN。","混凝土結構太重，不可能在海上浮運。"],"optionsEn":["If the deck hangs freely from the pylons, it needs no damping devices in an earthquake.","A 61-strand stay has a breaking force of 61×150 mm²×1,770 MPa ≈ 16,200 kN.","Concrete structures are too heavy to float and tow at sea."],"answer":1,"explanation":"61 股鋼絞線斜索破斷力 = 61×150 mm²×1,770 MPa ≈ 16,200 kN。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"A 61-strand stay has a breaking force of 61×150 mm²×1,770 MPa ≈ 16,200 kN. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b012-v13-35","title":"雷擊、斜索火災與單索更換：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Lightning, stay fire and single-stay replacement: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"],"prerequisiteIds":["b012-v13-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「M1 塔斜索」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Stays at pylon M1” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以非線性動力分析模擬各代表性斜索的突然斷失，檢查鄰索應力比、橋面彎矩與塔的反應；雷擊防護系統依相關防雷標準驗證接地與導通，更換斜索時以荷重計與測量監控臨時索力與橋面線形。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Simulate sudden loss of representative stays with nonlinear dynamic analysis, checking neighbour stress ratios, deck moments and pylon response; verify lightning protection grounding and continuity under the relevant lightning standard, and monitor temporary forces and deck profile with load cells and survey during stay replacement. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：每座斜張橋都應有書面的斷索應變計畫：交通管制、臨時支撐、備品來源與更換程序；防雷與防火措施要列入斜索系統規格，並在檢查中確認接地完整。","observationEn":"Site practice: Every cable-stayed bridge should have a written stay-loss contingency plan covering traffic control, temporary support, spare supply and replacement procedure; lightning and fire protection belong in the stay-system specification, with earthing checked during inspections.","failure":"注意干擾：未設計斷索工況時，一根斜索失效可能使鄰索超載連鎖斷裂；HDPE 套管可燃，若未考慮雷擊或車輛火災，火勢可能沿套管蔓延，使鋼絞線高溫失去強度。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Without a stay-loss case, one failure can overload neighbours in a chain; HDPE ducts are combustible, and without consideration of lightning or vehicle fire, flames can spread along the duct and heat the strands until they lose strength. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b012-v13-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以非線性動力分析模擬各代表性斜索的突然斷失，檢查鄰索應力比、橋面彎矩與塔的反應；雷擊防護系統依相關防雷標準驗證接地與導通，更換斜索時以荷重計與測量監控臨時索力與橋面線形。","textEn":"Simulate sudden loss of representative stays with nonlinear dynamic analysis, checking neighbour stress ratios, deck moments and pylon response; verify lightning protection grounding and continuity under the relevant lightning standard, and monitor temporary forces and deck profile with load cells and survey during stay replacement.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]},{"id":"b012-v13-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"每座斜張橋都應有書面的斷索應變計畫：交通管制、臨時支撐、備品來源與更換程序；防雷與防火措施要列入斜索系統規格，並在檢查中確認接地完整。","textEn":"Every cable-stayed bridge should have a written stay-loss contingency plan covering traffic control, temporary support, spare supply and replacement procedure; lightning and fire protection belong in the stay-system specification, with earthing checked during inspections.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「雷擊、斜索火災與單索更換」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Lightning, stay fire and single-stay replacement\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","平衡懸臂只要最後兩側長度相同，中間的施工順序不重要。","以非線性動力分析模擬各代表性斜索的突然斷失，檢查鄰索應力比、橋面彎矩與塔的反應。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","In balanced cantilever erection only the final equal lengths matter, not the order in between.","Simulate sudden loss of representative stays with nonlinear dynamic analysis, checking neighbour stress ratios, deck moments and pylon response."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以非線性動力分析模擬各代表性斜索的突然斷失，檢查鄰索應力比、橋面彎矩與塔的反應；雷擊防護系統依相關防雷標準驗證接地與導通，更換斜索時以荷重計與測量監控臨時索力與橋面線形。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Simulate sudden loss of representative stays with nonlinear dynamic analysis, checking neighbour stress ratios, deck moments and pylon response; verify lightning protection grounding and continuity under the relevant lightning standard, and monitor temporary forces and deck profile with load cells and survey during stay replacement. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b012-v13-36","title":"雷擊、斜索火災與單索更換：失效診斷","titleEn":"Lightning, stay fire and single-stay replacement: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"],"prerequisiteIds":["b012-v13-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「M1 塔斜索」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Stays at pylon M1” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"未設計斷索工況時，一根斜索失效可能使鄰索超載連鎖斷裂；HDPE 套管可燃，若未考慮雷擊或車輛火災，火勢可能沿套管蔓延，使鋼絞線高溫失去強度。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Without a stay-loss case, one failure can overload neighbours in a chain; HDPE ducts are combustible, and without consideration of lightning or vehicle fire, flames can spread along the duct and heat the strands until they lose strength. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：斜索斷失是斜張橋必須設計的意外工況：斷索瞬間釋放的能量使相鄰斜索與橋面產生動力放大，力量重新分配到鄰索；設計必須確認鄰索與橋面在這個工況下不會連鎖破壞，同時要有可以在交通管制下更換單索的程序。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Stay loss is an accidental case every cable-stayed bridge must be designed for: the sudden release of energy dynamically amplifies the response of neighbouring stays and the deck as force redistributes; design must confirm that neighbours and deck do not fail progressively and that a single stay can be replaced under traffic management.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「斜索是由許多鋼絞線組成的，所以整根斜索不可能突然失效。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Because a stay is made of many strands, the whole stay can never fail suddenly.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b012-v13-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"未設計斷索工況時，一根斜索失效可能使鄰索超載連鎖斷裂；HDPE 套管可燃，若未考慮雷擊或車輛火災，火勢可能沿套管蔓延，使鋼絞線高溫失去強度。","textEn":"Without a stay-loss case, one failure can overload neighbours in a chain; HDPE ducts are combustible, and without consideration of lightning or vehicle fire, flames can spread along the duct and heat the strands until they lose strength.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]},{"id":"b012-v13-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「雷擊、斜索火災與單索更換」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Lightning, stay fire and single-stay replacement\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["未設計斷索工況時，一根斜索失效可能使鄰索超載連鎖斷裂；HDPE 套管可燃，若未考慮雷擊或車輛火災，火勢可能沿套管蔓延，使鋼絞線高溫失去強度。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","高強度海工混凝土在 120 年內不需要任何耐久性檢測。"],"optionsEn":["Without a stay-loss case, one failure can overload neighbours in a chain.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","High-strength marine concrete needs no durability testing over 120 years."],"answer":0,"explanation":"未設計斷索工況時，一根斜索失效可能使鄰索超載連鎖斷裂；HDPE 套管可燃，若未考慮雷擊或車輛火災，火勢可能沿套管蔓延，使鋼絞線高溫失去強度。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Without a stay-loss case, one failure can overload neighbours in a chain; HDPE ducts are combustible, and without consideration of lightning or vehicle fire, flames can spread along the duct and heat the strands until they lose strength. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b012-v13-37","title":"海洋混凝土耐久與 120 年檢查維護：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Marine concrete durability and 120-year inspection: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"],"prerequisiteIds":["b012-v13-36"],"objective":"說明「浪濺區混凝土」如何影響里翁—安提里翁大橋的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Splash-zone concrete” governs force, deformation or durability in “Rion–Antirion Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"大橋設計使用年限 120 年，營運單位公開的檢查與維護手冊經獨立工程師核可，將混凝土耐久列為主要風險之一：海水化學侵蝕、氯離子引致的鋼筋腐蝕與二氧化碳造成的中性化腐蝕。防護依暴露分區規定保護層厚度與混凝土性質；營運期以平板電腦搭配客製軟體做目視檢查，缺陷分類後標在電子圖上，並以定期試驗量測氯離子滲透與擴散係數以推估剩餘壽命。檢查方式涵蓋橋面檢修車、墩座吊籃、繩索技術檢查塔與斜索，以及以水下遙控載具或潛水員檢查墩座與沖刷防護。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「浪濺區混凝土」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The bridge has a 120-year design life, and the operator’s inspection and maintenance manual, approved by the independent engineer, lists concrete durability as a main risk: chemical attack by seawater, chloride-induced reinforcement corrosion and carbonation-induced corrosion. Protection relies on cover and concrete properties defined by exposure zone; in service, visual inspections use tablet PCs with customised software, classify defects and mark them on electronic drawings, and regular tests measure chloride penetration and diffusivity to estimate remaining life. Access includes the deck gantry, pier-base cradles, rope access for pylons and stays, and ROVs or divers for pier bases and scour protection. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Splash-zone concrete” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：Fick 第二定律 C(x,t) = C_s·[1 − erf(x/(2√(D·t)))]。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Fick’s second law C(x,t) = C_s·[1 − erf(x/(2√(D·t)))].","failure":"常見誤解：「高強度海工混凝土在 120 年內不需要任何耐久性檢測。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"High-strength marine concrete needs no durability testing over 120 years.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「浪濺區混凝土」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Splash-zone concrete”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b012-v13-37-k1","title":"海洋混凝土耐久與 120 年檢查維護","titleEn":"Marine concrete durability and 120-year inspection","text":"大橋設計使用年限 120 年，營運單位公開的檢查與維護手冊經獨立工程師核可，將混凝土耐久列為主要風險之一：海水化學侵蝕、氯離子引致的鋼筋腐蝕與二氧化碳造成的中性化腐蝕。防護依暴露分區規定保護層厚度與混凝土性質；營運期以平板電腦搭配客製軟體做目視檢查，缺陷分類後標在電子圖上，並以定期試驗量測氯離子滲透與擴散係數以推估剩餘壽命。","textEn":"The bridge has a 120-year design life, and the operator’s inspection and maintenance manual, approved by the independent engineer, lists concrete durability as a main risk: chemical attack by seawater, chloride-induced reinforcement corrosion and carbonation-induced corrosion. Protection relies on cover and concrete properties defined by exposure zone; in service, visual inspections use tablet PCs with customised software, classify defects and mark them on electronic drawings, and regular tests measure chloride penetration and diffusivity to estimate remaining life.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]},{"id":"b012-v13-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：高強度海工混凝土在 120 年內不需要任何耐久性檢測。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: High-strength marine concrete needs no durability testing over 120 years. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「海洋混凝土耐久與 120 年檢查維護」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Marine concrete durability and 120-year inspection\" is correct?","options":["高強度海工混凝土在 120 年內不需要任何耐久性檢測。","大橋設計使用年限 120 年，營運單位公開的檢查與維護手冊經獨立工程師核可，將混凝土耐久列為主要風險之一：海水化學侵蝕、氯離子引致的鋼筋腐蝕與二氧化碳造成的中性化腐蝕。","抗震設計的最佳做法永遠是把結構做得更強、更固定。"],"optionsEn":["High-strength marine concrete needs no durability testing over 120 years.","The bridge has a 120-year design life, and the operator’s inspection and maintenance manual, approved by the independent engineer, lists concrete durability as a main risk: chemical attack by seawater, chloride-induced reinforcement corrosion and carbonation-induced corrosion.","The best seismic design is always to make the structure stronger and more rigidly fixed."],"answer":1,"explanation":"大橋設計使用年限 120 年，營運單位公開的檢查與維護手冊經獨立工程師核可，將混凝土耐久列為主要風險之一：海水化學侵蝕、氯離子引致的鋼筋腐蝕與二氧化碳造成的中性化腐蝕。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The bridge has a 120-year design life, and the operator’s inspection and maintenance manual, approved by the independent engineer, lists concrete durability as a main risk: chemical attack by seawater, chloride-induced reinforcement corrosion and carbonation-induced corrosion. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b012-v13-38","title":"海洋混凝土耐久與 120 年檢查維護：定量估算","titleEn":"Marine concrete durability and 120-year inspection: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"],"prerequisiteIds":["b012-v13-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「浪濺區混凝土」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Splash-zone concrete” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：Fick 第二定律 C(x,t) = C_s·[1 − erf(x/(2√(D·t)))]。取 C_s = 0.6%（膠結料重）、D = 5×10⁻¹³ m²/s、t = 50 年、x = 60 mm：2√(Dt) ≈ 0.056 m，erf(1.068) ≈ 0.869，C ≈ 0.6×0.131 ≈ 0.079%，低於約 0.4% 的腐蝕起始門檻；若 D = 2×10⁻¹² m²/s，C ≈ 0.27%。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Fick’s second law C(x,t) = C_s·[1 − erf(x/(2√(D·t)))]. With C_s = 0.6% by binder mass, D = 5×10⁻¹³ m²/s, t = 50 years and x = 60 mm, 2√(Dt) ≈ 0.056 m, erf(1.068) ≈ 0.869 and C ≈ 0.6×0.131 ≈ 0.079%, below a corrosion threshold of about 0.4%; with D = 2×10⁻¹² m²/s, C ≈ 0.27%. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在各暴露分區設固定取樣點，定期鑽取粉末量測不同深度的氯離子濃度，擬合表面濃度與擴散係數，並與上一輪結果比較；同時以保護層量測與半電池電位檢查高風險區，所有結果進入單一資料庫並自動產生報告。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Fix sampling points in each exposure zone, periodically drill dust at several depths for chloride concentration, fit surface concentration and diffusivity and compare with the previous round; check high-risk areas with cover surveys and half-cell potential, entering all results into a single database with automatic reporting.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b012-v13-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"Fick 第二定律 C(x,t) = C_s·[1 − erf(x/(2√(D·t)))]。取 C_s = 0.6%（膠結料重）、D = 5×10⁻¹³ m²/s、t = 50 年、x = 60 mm：2√(Dt) ≈ 0.056 m，erf(1.068) ≈ 0.869，C ≈ 0.6×0.131 ≈ 0.079%，低於約 0.4% 的腐蝕起始門檻；若 D = 2×10⁻¹² m²/s，C ≈ 0.27%。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Fick’s second law C(x,t) = C_s·[1 − erf(x/(2√(D·t)))]. With C_s = 0.6% by binder mass, D = 5×10⁻¹³ m²/s, t = 50 years and x = 60 mm, 2√(Dt) ≈ 0.056 m, erf(1.068) ≈ 0.869 and C ≈ 0.6×0.131 ≈ 0.079%, below a corrosion threshold of about 0.4%; with D = 2×10⁻¹² m²/s, C ≈ 0.27%. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]},{"id":"b012-v13-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「海洋混凝土耐久與 120 年檢查維護」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Marine concrete durability and 120-year inspection\", which statement holds?","options":["軟弱海床上的大橋基礎一定要用長樁打到岩盤。","深海的礫石墊層只是填料，平整度要求可以放寬。","Fick 第二定律 C(x,t) = C_s·[1 − erf(x/(2√(D·t)))]。"],"optionsEn":["Bridge foundations on soft seabed must always use long piles driven to rock.","A deep-water gravel bed is just fill, so its flatness can be relaxed.","Fick’s second law C(x,t) = C_s·[1 − erf(x/(2√(D·t)))]."],"answer":2,"explanation":"Fick 第二定律 C(x,t) = C_s·[1 − erf(x/(2√(D·t)))]。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Fick’s second law C(x,t) = C_s·[1 − erf(x/(2√(D·t)))]. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b012-v13-39","title":"海洋混凝土耐久與 120 年檢查維護：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Marine concrete durability and 120-year inspection: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"],"prerequisiteIds":["b012-v13-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「浪濺區混凝土」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Splash-zone concrete” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在各暴露分區設固定取樣點，定期鑽取粉末量測不同深度的氯離子濃度，擬合表面濃度與擴散係數，並與上一輪結果比較；同時以保護層量測與半電池電位檢查高風險區，所有結果進入單一資料庫並自動產生報告。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Fix sampling points in each exposure zone, periodically drill dust at several depths for chloride concentration, fit surface concentration and diffusivity and compare with the previous round; check high-risk areas with cover surveys and half-cell potential, entering all results into a single database with automatic reporting. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：檢查與維護手冊要明訂各構件的檢查週期、取樣位置、允收門檻與觸發維修的條件，並把檢查結果由結構維護工程師、原設計者與專業供應商共同評估後決定行動。","observationEn":"Site practice: The inspection and maintenance manual should set inspection intervals, sampling positions, acceptance thresholds and repair triggers for each component, with findings assessed jointly by the structural maintenance engineers, the original designer and specialist suppliers before action is decided.","failure":"注意干擾：若只做目視檢查而沒有氯離子剖面，腐蝕起始前的劣化趨勢無法察覺，等到鏽水與剝落出現時修復範圍已大；水下墩座與沖刷防護若缺乏定期檢查，局部損壞可能長期未被發現。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Visual inspection without chloride profiles misses the trend before corrosion starts, so by the time rust staining and spalling appear the repair area is large; without regular underwater inspection, local damage to pier bases and scour protection can go unnoticed for years. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b012-v13-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在各暴露分區設固定取樣點，定期鑽取粉末量測不同深度的氯離子濃度，擬合表面濃度與擴散係數，並與上一輪結果比較；同時以保護層量測與半電池電位檢查高風險區，所有結果進入單一資料庫並自動產生報告。","textEn":"Fix sampling points in each exposure zone, periodically drill dust at several depths for chloride concentration, fit surface concentration and diffusivity and compare with the previous round; check high-risk areas with cover surveys and half-cell potential, entering all results into a single database with automatic reporting.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]},{"id":"b012-v13-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"檢查與維護手冊要明訂各構件的檢查週期、取樣位置、允收門檻與觸發維修的條件，並把檢查結果由結構維護工程師、原設計者與專業供應商共同評估後決定行動。","textEn":"The inspection and maintenance manual should set inspection intervals, sampling positions, acceptance thresholds and repair triggers for each component, with findings assessed jointly by the structural maintenance engineers, the original designer and specialist suppliers before action is decided.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「海洋混凝土耐久與 120 年檢查維護」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Marine concrete durability and 120-year inspection\"?","options":["在各暴露分區設固定取樣點，定期鑽取粉末量測不同深度的氯離子濃度，擬合表面濃度與擴散係數，並與上一輪結果比較。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","感測器越多、取樣越快，監測系統就一定越有用。"],"optionsEn":["Fix sampling points in each exposure zone, periodically drill dust at several depths for chloride concentration, fit surface concentration and diffusivity and compare with the previous round.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","More sensors and faster sampling always make a monitoring system more useful."],"answer":0,"explanation":"在各暴露分區設固定取樣點，定期鑽取粉末量測不同深度的氯離子濃度，擬合表面濃度與擴散係數，並與上一輪結果比較；同時以保護層量測與半電池電位檢查高風險區，所有結果進入單一資料庫並自動產生報告。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Fix sampling points in each exposure zone, periodically drill dust at several depths for chloride concentration, fit surface concentration and diffusivity and compare with the previous round; check high-risk areas with cover surveys and half-cell potential, entering all results into a single database with automatic reporting. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b012-v13-40","title":"海洋混凝土耐久與 120 年檢查維護：失效診斷","titleEn":"Marine concrete durability and 120-year inspection: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"],"prerequisiteIds":["b012-v13-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「浪濺區混凝土」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Splash-zone concrete” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若只做目視檢查而沒有氯離子剖面，腐蝕起始前的劣化趨勢無法察覺，等到鏽水與剝落出現時修復範圍已大；水下墩座與沖刷防護若缺乏定期檢查，局部損壞可能長期未被發現。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Visual inspection without chloride profiles misses the trend before corrosion starts, so by the time rust staining and spalling appear the repair area is large; without regular underwater inspection, local damage to pier bases and scour protection can go unnoticed for years. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：檢查方式涵蓋橋面檢修車、墩座吊籃、繩索技術檢查塔與斜索，以及以水下遙控載具或潛水員檢查墩座與沖刷防護。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Access includes the deck gantry, pier-base cradles, rope access for pylons and stays, and ROVs or divers for pier bases and scour protection.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「高強度海工混凝土在 120 年內不需要任何耐久性檢測。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"High-strength marine concrete needs no durability testing over 120 years.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b012-v13-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若只做目視檢查而沒有氯離子剖面，腐蝕起始前的劣化趨勢無法察覺，等到鏽水與剝落出現時修復範圍已大；水下墩座與沖刷防護若缺乏定期檢查，局部損壞可能長期未被發現。","textEn":"Visual inspection without chloride profiles misses the trend before corrosion starts, so by the time rust staining and spalling appear the repair area is large; without regular underwater inspection, local damage to pier bases and scour protection can go unnoticed for years.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]},{"id":"b012-v13-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「海洋混凝土耐久與 120 年檢查維護」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Marine concrete durability and 120-year inspection\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","若只做目視檢查而沒有氯離子剖面，腐蝕起始前的劣化趨勢無法察覺，等到鏽水與剝落出現時修復範圍已大；水下墩座與沖刷防護若缺乏定期檢查，局部損壞可能長期未被發現。","抗震設計的最佳做法永遠是把結構做得更強、更固定。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Visual inspection without chloride profiles misses the trend before corrosion starts, so by the time rust staining and spalling appear the repair area is large.","The best seismic design is always to make the structure stronger and more rigidly fixed."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若只做目視檢查而沒有氯離子剖面，腐蝕起始前的劣化趨勢無法察覺，等到鏽水與剝落出現時修復範圍已大；水下墩座與沖刷防護若缺乏定期檢查，局部損壞可能長期未被發現。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Visual inspection without chloride profiles misses the trend before corrosion starts, so by the time rust staining and spalling appear the repair area is large; without regular underwater inspection, local damage to pier bases and scour protection can go unnoticed for years. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v13s-gefyra-design-construction","v13s-gefyra-monitoring-maintenance","v13s-freyssinet-stay-protection","v13s-wiki-rion-antirion"],"curriculumVersion":13,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
